                                                (SerializePayloadSorted, camelCase + recursive
                                                key-sort) is used by BOTH CreateSignedSnapshot
                                                (:118-120) and VerifySnapshot (:161-169);
                                                WitnessSnapshot carries no format-version field and
                                                VerifySnapshot has no legacy (PascalCase/unsorted)
                                                fallback, so any snapshot signed by a pre-change
                                                Windows build fails Ed25519 verification and is
                                                reported as tampered — a false "tampered" claim
                                                against genuine evidence (Criticality High stands;
                                                arguably Critical under the forgeable/false-evidence
                                                rule, since the tool impeaches its own attestations).
                                                Mitigating context the adjudicator should weigh: the
                                                repo is pre-release and no third-party snapshots
                                                exist yet, so "wontfix legacy verification + add a
                                                formatVersion NOW" is a defensible resolution —
                                                versioning the snapshot before first release (S
                                                effort: add `formatVersion: 2` to WitnessSnapshot and
                                                reject-with-reason instead of reporting tampered for
                                                unknown versions) satisfies the delta's intent
                                                without a legacy re-serializer. Cross-ref E011
                                                remains correct and separate (payload key-order
                                                interop). Validation: sign a fixture with the OLD
                                                serialization, assert verify yields
                                                "unsupported format version", never "tampered".
- **Tag:**              OBSERVED (workflow agent; Claude spot-checked the quoted code, not run).

