- **[D003]**            No TLS Pinning for Leak Collector Communication
- **FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** Pinning mechanism exists; unconfigured pins now surface caveat in result and transportPinning status.
- **Criticality:**      Critical (CA compromise or on-path TLS proxy can forge leak
                        verdicts); user made aware.
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/LeakDetector.swift:44-49
- **Issue:**            `collectorSession` uses ephemeral URLSession but no `SecTrust` or
                        certificate pinning. A CA compromise or enterprise TLS proxy can
                        intercept collector communication and return forged leak verdicts
                        with fake cryptographic attestations. Undermines the entire leak
                        detection chain of custody.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Add public-key pinning for the collector server.
                        [Fix 2] Implement certificate transparency enforcement.

                       - **Tool Name**            [Opencode]
                       - **Date**                 7-9-2026
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       N/A
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   TLS pinning is absent for both leak-collector and
                                                   Keygen API calls. An attacker with a CA compromise or
                                                   root trust injection can intercept collector
                                                   communications. Fix: add certificate/public-key pinning
                                                   via `NSPinnedDomains` (macOS) or
                                                   `HttpClientHandler.ServerCertificateCustomValidationCallback`
                                                   (Windows). Not urgent — the collector signature
                                                   provides cryptographic attestation independent of
                                                   transport security.


                       - **Tool Name**            [Codex]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree with revisions
                       - **Disagree Basis**       macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/LeakDetector.swift:44-49 —
                                                  Production-source inspection shows:
                                                  `collectorSession` uses ephemeral URLSession but
                                                  no `SecTrust` or certificate pinning. A CA
                                                  compromise or enterprise TLS proxy can intercept
                                                  collector communication and return forged leak
                                                  verdicts with fake cryptographic attestations.
                                                  Undermines the entire leak detection chain of
                                                  custody.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Retitle to pinning unconfigured by default;
                                                  require production pins or force inconclusive.

                       - **Tool Name**            [Claude]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree with revisions
                       - **Disagree Basis**       The "no SecTrust/pinning" claim is now partly
                                                  stale: a pinning MECHANISM exists
                                                  (CollectorPinningDelegate/makeCollectorSession
                                                  :101-107; transportPinning posture; a pin/PKI
                                                  failure forces .inconclusive :52-55,180-182). But
                                                  configuredPins() defaults EMPTY — no pins are
                                                  hardcoded (LeakDetector.swift:417-422, "OWNER
                                                  DELIVERABLE") — so posture is .notConfigured and
                                                  only standard TLS applies. A CA compromise or
                                                  enterprise TLS proxy still forges a leak verdict
                                                  out of the box.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Retitle "pinning present but unconfigured by
                                                  default." Ship the real collector SPKI pins as a
                                                  deployment input and force .inconclusive for
                                                  privacy-sensitive runs (leak/witness) when pins are
                                                  absent. Critical: forgeable leak verdict under
                                                  TLS-MITM; couples with D004 (not verdict-gating)
                                                  and D011 (no trust anchor).

