- **[E008]**            **FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** Added `.reserved` to macOS `isUsableDNSServer` exclusion set to match Windows parity. Link-local deliberately NOT excluded per RFC 8106 RDNSS which permits link-local resolver addresses.
- **Criticality:**      Low-Medium (macOS can adopt a link-local/reserved address as a resolver and
                        use it
                        as a comparison/leak target); analysis 2026-07-09.
- **Location:**         macOS NetworkKeyState.swift:194-202 vs Windows NetworkKeyState.cs:137-150.
- **Issue:**            macOS excludes only `documentation, unspecified, invalid, multicast`.
                        Windows also
                        excludes `Reserved` and `LinkLocal`. On macOS a `fe80::`/`169.254.x` entry from
                        `scutil` passes `isUsableDNSServer` and gets queried/compared.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** None. Claude-verified.
- **Fix(es):**          [1] Add `.reserved` and `.linkLocal` to the macOS exclusion set.

                       - **Tool Name**            [syxx-researcher]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-10
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       N/A
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   CONFIRMED still open, with two corrections. (1) Line
                                                  drift: the macOS exclusion set is now
                                                  NetworkKeyState.swift:222-230 (not :194-202) —
                                                  `case .documentation, .unspecified, .invalid,
                                                  .multicast: return false`; Windows
                                                  NetworkKeyState.cs:141-149 additionally excludes
                                                  `Reserved` and `LinkLocal`, per its own comment
                                                  ("a link-local address can never be an off-link
                                                  recursive resolver"). (2) Fix [1] should not be a
                                                  blind copy of Windows: RFC 8106 RDNSS explicitly
                                                  permits link-local resolver addresses, and home
                                                  routers commonly advertise fe80:: resolvers —
                                                  blanket `.linkLocal` exclusion can DROP the real
                                                  system resolver and blind comparison/leak probes
                                                  (honest `.unknown`, but lost visibility). Note the
                                                  practical macOS exposure is already narrow: scoped
                                                  forms like `fe80::1%en0` fail inet_pton and
                                                  classify `.invalid` (IPClassifier.swift:17-24), so
                                                  only zoneless fe80, 169.254.x IPv4, and Reserved
                                                  (240/4, 192.0.0.0/24; fec0::/10 is Windows-only
                                                  placeholder territory) actually pass today.
                                                  Revised fix: add `.reserved` to the macOS set to
                                                  match Windows; decide the link-local contract
                                                  deliberately on BOTH platforms (exclude IPv4
                                                  169.254.x; for IPv6 fe80 either support zone-
                                                  scoped queries or exclude with an explicit
                                                  evidence note) rather than silently diverging in
                                                  either direction. Criticality Low-Medium is right
                                                  (no false verdict; a bogus resolver becomes a
                                                  probe target that fails → inconclusive). Not a
                                                  duplicate; B025 cross-ref at DELTAS.md:1323
                                                  already points here. Effort S. Validation: unit
                                                  fixtures for fe80::1, fe80::1%en0, 169.254.1.1,
                                                  fec0:0:0:ffff::1, 240.0.0.1 asserting identical
                                                  accept/reject on both platforms.
- **Tag:**              OBSERVED (Claude-verified).

