- **[B041]**            **FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code), already resolved.** Report.swift:176-179 now renders an "EXPOSURE FINDINGS" block iterating `conclusion.advisories` with title and detail.
- **Criticality:**      Non-critical currently (report layer unwired; GUI still shows advisories at
                        OverallVerdictView.swift:200); becomes a missed-communication / false-"nothing
                        found" defect the moment renderText is wired to a CLI or export. User to be made
                        aware.
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/Synthesis/Report.swift:111-155 (`renderText` renders
                        Verdict/Likelihood/Belief/FACTS/WHY/SECTIONS/NEXT STEPS/SECOND OPINION — no
                        advisories block); Windows twin Report.cs:92-135 (`RenderText`, same omission);
                        producer at Synthesizer.swift:394-406 / Synthesizer.swift:534-539 populates
                        `Conclusion.advisories`.
- **Issue:**            `openResolver` is deliberately routed to `Conclusion.advisories` (an
                        EXPOSURE channel outside the tamper verdict) and can carry `severity: .high`
                        ("Possible open-resolver / amplification exposure"). `renderText` renders
                        `conclusion.evidence` (WHY) but never `conclusion.advisories`, so the entire
                        advisory channel — currently the only real security-hygiene finding the
                        pipeline emits — is invisible in the report the API bills as "every fact the
                        run gathered." A real, high-severity finding produced by the engine reaches
                        the GUI but not this report surface: a signal that fails to reach the user
                        through the report path.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** Same theme as B039 (report layer drops a real signal). Distinct channel
                        (advisories, not datapoints). Not otherwise tracked.
