- **[C010]**            version.bind Escalated From Tilt-Only to Section-Gating on Windows —
**FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code), already resolved.** Synthesizer.cs now emits EvidenceItem only for version.bind, never gates section status.
**FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code), already resolved.** Synthesizer.cs now emits EvidenceItem only for version.bind, never gates section status.
                        Spoofable Banner Suppresses a Warranted Clean Verdict (macOS vs Windows)
- **Criticality:**      Critical; false-confidence-direction divergence driven by forgeable evidence;
                        analysis 2026-07-10, verified by code read (not a live version.bind probe run).
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/Synthesis/Synthesizer.swift:206-212;
                        Windows/Syxx.Kit/Synthesis/Synthesizer.cs:269-283
- **Issue:**            F2 version.bind is documented as TILT-ONLY: macOS emits a weak (weight 0.4,
                        interception) EvidenceItem when a would-be public recursive answers with a
                        local-forwarder banner but adds NO section sub-status — the explicit contract
                        at Synthesizer.swift:205-206 ("it does NOT change the section status (no
                        `.positive`, no gate)"). Windows VIOLATES that contract: on
                        `vb.ForwarderOnPublicPath` it does `subs.Add(SectionStatus.Positive)`
                        (Synthesizer.cs:276), making the whole Prophet section Positive. Because
                        `SynthesisEngine` only grants CLEAN support for `.Negative` sections
                        (SynthesisEngine.cs:154-156; .swift:184-186), a Positive Prophet withholds
                        the clean support Prophet would otherwise contribute AND leaves the 0.4
                        interception hypothesis undamped. Net: the SAME spoofable CHAOS banner
                        (any resolver/middlebox can return any version.bind TXT — RFC 4892 is
                        advisory, values are attacker-controllable) leaves macOS able to name a clean
                        verdict but pushes Windows off "clean" toward inconclusive/interception. This
                        is exactly the on-path adversary Syxx exists to catch feeding forgeable
                        evidence into a verdict on one platform only. Secondary in the same block:
                        Windows maps `Withheld` (hardened resolver, "not an error, not clean" per
                        VersionBindProbe.cs) to `.Negative` (clean-supporting) at Synthesizer.cs:282,
                        another §1 honesty slip macOS does not make (macOS adds no sub for any
                        version.bind status).
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** Not covered by C005 (gathering, now fixed via ProbePlan). Adjacent to B020/
                        B021 calibration work (both platforms) but this is a platform DIVERGENCE, not
                        a shared miscalibration. Weight 0.4 confirmed both: Conclusion.swift:253,
                        Conclusion.cs:190.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Make Windows match the macOS contract: emit the EvidenceItem only,
                        never `subs.Add(...)` for version.bind (delete the Positive on forwarder and
                        the two `.Negative` adds; version.bind must contribute zero section status).
                        [Fix 2] Move the F2 mapping into a single shared Kit helper so the tilt-only
                        contract can't drift per platform again (aligns with the C005 root cause).
- **§3 test:**          Feed `SectionInputs` with ONLY `versionBind = forwarderOnPublicPath:true`
                        and all other sections Negative/clean, on BOTH platforms; assert byte-identical
                        Conclusion.verdict and that verdict == Clean (or, if the design says
                        inconclusive, that BOTH platforms agree). FAILURE CASE: with the current
                        Windows code the verdicts differ (macOS clean-capable, Windows clean-blocked)
                        → the parity assertion must fail today, proving it detects the divergence.
                        Add a second case: version.bind `Withheld` alone must NOT push either platform
                        toward clean.

- **Code Sample:**      [

                        // macOS Synthesizer.swift:207-212 — TILT-ONLY (no subs.append)
                        if let vb = versionBind, vb.forwarderOnPublicPath, let banner = vb.banner {
                            ev.append(EvidenceItem(section: .prophet,
                                evidenceId: .resolverBannerAnomaly, ...))
                            // (no subs.append — never gates)
                        }

                        // Windows Synthesizer.cs:271-282 — GATES the section (BUG)
                        if (vb.ForwarderOnPublicPath) {
                            ev.Add(...);
                            subs.Add(SectionStatus.Positive);   // <-- violates tilt-only contract
                        }
                        else if (vb.Status == VersionBindResultStatus.Disclosed)
                            subs.Add(SectionStatus.Negative);   // <-- macOS adds nothing here
                        else if (vb.Status == VersionBindResultStatus.Untested) { }
                        else subs.Add(SectionStatus.Negative);  // <-- Withheld reads as clean

                        ]

- **Re-confirmed:**     2026-07-11 (five-agent audit, finding #61): still present. Windows
                        version.bind `ForwarderOnPublicPath -> subs.Add(Positive)`
                        (Synthesizer.cs:271-282) gates the whole Prophet section from a spoofable
                        CHAOS banner (and maps Withheld->Negative/clean); macOS
                        (Synthesizer.swift:207-212) is tilt-only. Emit the EvidenceItem only; zero
                        section status for any version.bind state. Updated in place, not re-filed.


