- **[F010]**            "Start your story anew" Button Disconnected — No Longer Resets Panel Views
- **Criticality:**      Non-critical; cosmetic/UX.
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxApp/ContentView.swift:41; macOS/Sources/SyxxApp/AppModel.swift:131-159
- **Issue:**            The "Start your story anew" button in the header bar calls
                        `model.resetAll()` but no longer resets the individual panel views.
                        The button exists and is visible, but clicking it has no visible effect —
                        panel state (input fields, output text, running indicators) remains
                        unchanged. The user reports it was "disconnected" and the intent was to
                        reset each panel to its just-opened state.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** Not covered elsewhere.
- **Fix(es):**          Verify `resetAll()` in AppModel.swift actually clears all `@Published`
                        properties. If the panel views hold local `@State` that isn't driven by
                        the model, migrate that state to the model or add a `@Published` reset
                        counter that views observe and respond to.
- **Code Sample:**      [

                        // ContentView.swift:41
                        ClearContentButton { model.resetAll() }

                        // AppModel.swift:131-159 — resetAll() clears model properties but
                        // panel views may hold independent @State that isn't reset.

                        ]

