- **[A034]**            Collector :53 Has No Rate Limit / Fresh Conn Per Packet / No Dedup — Write
                        DoS
- **Criticality:**      Critical (collector degradation / dropped observations — auto-enhanced from
                        Med per server-side criticality rule 1).
- **Location:**         Server/syxx_server/dns_authoritative.py:175-190;
                        Server/syxx_server/leak.py:110-122; Server/syxx_server/db.py:272-282
- **Issue:**            The collector :53 has no per-source rate limit; every in-zone packet opens a
                        fresh SQLite connection; a known-token cleartext replay produces unbounded
                        INSERTs (no dedup) → write contention and dropped observations, degrading
                        the collector for real leak tests.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** Cross-ref A009 residual.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Rate-limit :53 per source IP.
                        [Fix 2] Dedup per (token, resolver_ip).
                        [Fix 3] Cache token lookups instead of a fresh conn per packet.
- **Tag:**              CONFIRMED
**FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code), already resolved.** Per-source rate limit (`_dns_rate_ok`, 50/60s) gates DB writes; `leak_observation_add` deduplicates on `(token, resolver_ip, qtype)` via unique index; `_write_conn()` uses WAL-mode `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` for write isolation.

                       - **Tool Name**            [Claude]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-11
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       N/A
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   A034 is the A009 Fix 2 residual — the A009 fix
                                                  closed unknown-token writes, but known-token replay
                                                  is still unbounded, and the fresh-conn-per-packet
                                                  pattern will produce SQLite write-lock contention
                                                  under any real load. Fix 3 (cache token lookups)
                                                  is the highest-leverage improvement: it reduces
                                                  both the DB write frequency and the conn-per-packet
                                                  overhead. Criticality Critical (rule 1 — collector
                                                  degradation) is correct; a degraded collector means
                                                  legitimate leak probes return inconclusive.


                       - **Tool Name**            [Codex]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       Every valid known-token DNS hit creates a fresh
                                                  SQLite observation with no uniqueness constraint
                                                  at
                                                  Server/syxx_server/dns_authoritative.py:175-190,
                                                  leak.py:110-122, db.py:272-282. Token replay can
                                                  amplify writes/contention.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Rate-limit/deduplicate by
                                                  token,resolver,qtype,time bucket and bound
                                                  observations per token; invalid query-form packets
                                                  must not record.

                       - **Tool Name**            [Claude]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       Confirmed: leak.observe (leak.py:110-122) gates on
                                                  a known token (A009 closed unknown-token writes)
                                                  but then calls db.leak_observation_add + passive
                                                  record per hit with no uniqueness/dedup and no
                                                  per-source rate limit, each on a fresh connection.
                                                  Cleartext known-token replay drives unbounded
                                                  INSERTs -> SQLite write-lock contention -> dropped
                                                  observations. Critical (rule 1, collector
                                                  degradation -> false inconclusive on real leak
                                                  tests). A009 residual correct.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Dedup by (token,resolver_ip,qtype,time-bucket),
                                                  per-source-IP rate limit at :53, and cache token
                                                  lookups (Fix 3 is highest leverage: cuts both write
                                                  frequency and conn-per-packet cost). Priority: high.

