- **[C015]**            Same-CDN-Provider Softening Erases a Real Authoritative Divergence
- **Criticality:**      Non-critical (High); a true positive is downgraded to inconclusive when the
                        attacker origin shares the target's CDN block.
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/AuthoritativeVantage.swift:166-172;
                        macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/NetworkCohort.swift:82-91, 28-68
- **Issue:**            Same-CDN-provider softening downgrades a REAL authoritative divergence to
                        inconclusive when the attacker origin shares the target's CDN block
                        (Cloudflare /13, Akamai /10 = millions of IPs). A true positive becomes a
                        non-signal.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** Not B002 (distinct softening path).
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Same-provider should lower confidence / annotate, not erase
                        `diverges`.
                        [Fix 2] Require ASN/registrable corroboration before softening.
- **Tag:**              LIKELY

                       - **Tool Name**            [Claude]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-11
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       N/A
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   High criticality is correct (true positive erased
                                                  by CDN-block softening). The fix (same-provider
                                                  should annotate, not erase) is the correct direction.
                                                  The concern is real: Cloudflare /13 and Akamai /10
                                                  each span millions of IPs. Fix 2 (require ASN/
                                                  registrable corroboration before softening) is the
                                                  stronger form. The key insight is that "same CDN
                                                  provider" does not mean "same delivery network for
                                                  this customer" — an attacker using Cloudflare's
                                                  infrastructure to return a malicious IP can still be
                                                  on Cloudflare's ASN. LIKELY tag is appropriate since
                                                  the real-world frequency of this case depends on the
                                                  CDN block sizes used.

                       - **Tool Name**            [Codex]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/AuthoritativeVantage.swift:166-172;
                                                  macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/NetworkCohort.swift:82-91,
                                                  28-68 — Live-source inspection confirms the
                                                  operative behavior: Same-CDN-provider softening
                                                  downgrades a REAL authoritative divergence to
                                                  inconclusive when the attacker origin shares the
                                                  target's CDN block (Cloudflare /13, Akamai /10 =
                                                  millions of IPs). A true positive becomes a
                                                  non-signal.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Keep in C-domain; required disposition: [Fix 1]
                                                  Same-provider should lower confidence / annotate,
                                                  not erase `diverges`. [Fix 2] Require
                                                  ASN/registrable corroboration before softening.

                       - **Tool Name**            [Claude]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       Verified: NetworkCohort.sharedProvider (:82-91)
                                                  returns a provider only when EVERY IP in both
                                                  sets maps to the same single provider;
                                                  AuthoritativeVantage.swift:169-170 then softens
                                                  diverges -> inconclusive. Cloudflare
                                                  104.16.0.0/13 (~512K IPs) and Akamai
                                                  104.64.0.0/10 (~4M IPs) are single-provider
                                                  blocks, so an attacker hosting the malicious
                                                  origin inside the target's CDN block silently
                                                  erases a real divergence. Adversarial evasion,
                                                  not a random false positive.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Agree (High). Output is inconclusive not
                                                  'secure', so no honesty-spine false-secure, but
                                                  it is a defeatable missed detection an aware
                                                  attacker triggers by design. Prefer Fix 1 (keep
                                                  diverges, annotate/lower confidence) over
                                                  erasure; Fix 2 (ASN/registrable corroboration)
                                                  is the stronger gate.

