- **[D019]**            ContentWarp SSRF Guard TOCTOU/DNS-Rebind + Fails Open on No-Resolver
- **FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** Changed validateURLForSSRF to return validated IP; all fetches now pin to the validated IP with Host header, closing the TOCTOU/DNS-rebind window. Fail-closed on no-resolver/empty-answer was already in place.
- **Criticality:**      Non-critical (High); the SSRF guard is split by the hostile resolver and
                        fails open to "public."
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/ContentWarp.swift:312-347 (fetches :87, :118, :140,
                        :211; fail-open :326-328, :334-336)
- **Issue:**            The SSRF guard resolves the host via raw UDP but the fetch re-resolves via
                        `URLSession`, so the check and the fetch are split by the exact hostile
                        resolver Syxx assumes — a TOCTOU / DNS-rebind window. It also returns `true`
                        (public) on no-resolver / empty-answer, so it fails open.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** Cross-ref C006.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Resolve once and pin the fetch to the validated IP.
                        [Fix 2] Fail CLOSED (inconclusive) on no-resolver / empty answer.
- **Tag:**              CONFIRMED

                       - **Tool Name**            [Codex]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/ContentWarp.swift:312-347
                                                  (fetches :87, :118, :140, :211; fail-open
                                                  :326-328, :334-336) — Production-source inspection
                                                  shows: The SSRF guard resolves the host via raw
                                                  UDP but the fetch re-resolves via `URLSession`, so
                                                  the check and the fetch are split by the exact
                                                  hostile resolver Syxx assumes — a TOCTOU /
                                                  DNS-rebind window. It also returns `true` (public)
                                                  on no-resolver / empty-answer, so it fails open.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Retain the delta and its proposed fixes; require a
                                                  real production-path run and an adversarial or
                                                  failure case before closure.

                       - **Tool Name**            [Claude]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       Verified: validateURLForSSRF (:312-347) resolves
                                                  the host via raw UDP (:331-332) but the fetches
                                                  use URLSession.shared.data(from: targetURL)
                                                  (:87,:118,:140) which re-resolve independently
                                                  -> TOCTOU / DNS-rebind window controlled by the
                                                  exact hostile resolver Syxx assumes. Fail-open
                                                  confirmed: :328 (no resolver -> true) and
                                                  :334-336 (empty answer -> true).
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Agree (High). Fix 2 (fail CLOSED / inconclusive
                                                  on no-resolver or empty answer) is low-effort
                                                  and closes the fail-open hole immediately. Fix 1
                                                  (pin the fetch to the validated IP) is harder
                                                  with URLSession -- needs connect-to-IP + Host
                                                  header or a custom URLProtocol; call out the
                                                  effort.

