- **[D022]**            "Streaming" Log Readers OOM on Newline-Free Line; Aggregation Dicts
                        Unbounded
- **FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** Capped carry buffer at 1 MB in DNSCaptureReportGenerator.forEachLine and 2 MB in EndpointLogAnalyzer.streamLines (truncate on overrun). Bounded aggregation dicts to 50K distinct keys in DNSLogAnalyzer.analyze.
- **Criticality:**      Non-critical (Med); one newline-free line OOMs, and unbounded per-domain
                        dicts are worst on the exfil captures the tool most wants.
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/Cage/DNSCaptureReportGenerator.swift:289-309;
                        macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/Forensics/EndpointLogAnalyzer.swift:39-60;
                        macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/Forensics/DNSLogAnalyzer.swift:153-170
- **Issue:**            The "streaming" readers buffer `carry` until a newline, so one newline-free
                        line OOMs. Aggregation dictionaries are unbounded by domain cardinality
                        (highest on the exfil captures the tool most wants), and `bundledLists()` is
                        re-materialized per domain.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** Resource-safety; not previously tracked.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Cap the buffer (skip on overrun).
                        [Fix 2] Bound distinct-key retention (top-K).
                        [Fix 3] Hoist the bundled lists out of the per-domain loop.
