                       - **Disagree Basis**       Verified. Windows Trust/Trust.cs:123-139
                                                  (AnswerLedger.Load) and Sentinel.LoadSnapshot:239-250
                                                  deserialize plain JSON with no integrity check;
                                                  macOS Trust/AnswerLedger.swift:144-153 and
                                                  Trust/Sentinel.swift:90-93 likewise decode raw JSON
                                                  (files are 0600 owner-only but unsigned). A same-user
                                                  process can rewrite the baseline so Sentinel.Diff
                                                  yields no changes, suppressing config-change/drift
                                                  re-audit.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Signing helps ONLY if the MAC/signing key lives in
                                                  Keychain (macOS) / DPAPI (Windows), not beside the
                                                  file — else the attacker re-signs. Also: whoever can
                                                  write the baseline can DELETE it (Forget), forcing a
                                                  fresh baseline that captures the already-tampered
                                                  config, so integrity-tagging alone does not fully
                                                  close the hole; a durable fix corroborates against an
                                                  off-host reference. Med; missed-detection under a
                                                  local-attacker model, not a remote false-secure.

