                                                  returned at
                                                  Server/syxx_server/investigate.py:120-131 and
                                                  never checks the RRSIG type-covered field equals
                                                  DNSKEY (48).
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Parse RRSIG RDATA and bind it to the DNSKEY RRset;
                                                  presence still must not be described as
                                                  cryptographic validation.

                       - **Tool Name**            [Claude]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       Confirmed at investigate.py:123,130 — rrsigs is
                                                  every type-46 record returned, and observed =
                                                  has_dnskey and has_rrsig. The RRSIG typeCovered
                                                  field (first 2 rdata bytes) is never checked
                                                  against DNSKEY (48), so an RRSIG covering an
                                                  unrelated RRset plus any DNSKEY record yields
                                                  observed:true. The note "presence-only; not
                                                  cryptographically validated" (line 127) softens but
                                                  does not fix the observed:true claim. Critical as a
                                                  forgeable-evidence / false-positive posture.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Agree. Priority high. Parse the RRSIG RDATA and
