- **[C021]**            IPv4 Fragments Are Parsed as Complete UDP Datagrams
- **Criticality:**      Critical; non-initial fragments can be misread as UDP/DNS while fragmented
                        real DNS can be dropped or turned into false forensic records.
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/DNSCapture.swift:185-203;
                        Windows/Syxx.Kit/DNSCapture.cs:167-196
- **Issue:**            Neither parser checks MF or fragment offset before interpreting bytes after
                        IHL as a UDP header.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** Not previously tracked.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Reject all fragmented packets with an explicit coverage caveat or
                        implement bounded reassembly.
- **Code Sample:**      [

                        let protocolNumber = data[data.startIndex + 9]
                        // flags/fragment offset bytes 6-7 are never read

                        ]
- **Tag:**              CONFIRMED


                       - **Tool Name**            [Codex]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/DNSCapture.swift:185-203;
                                                  Windows/Syxx.Kit/DNSCapture.cs:167-196 —
                                                  Live-source inspection confirms the operative
                                                  behavior: Neither parser checks MF or fragment
                                                  offset before interpreting bytes after IHL as a
                                                  UDP header.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Keep in C-domain; required disposition: [Fix 1]
                                                  Reject all fragmented packets with an explicit
                                                  coverage caveat or implement bounded reassembly.

                       - **Tool Name**            [Claude]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       Confirmed both platforms. The IPv4 path
                                                  (macOS:244-262; Windows:230-257) reads
                                                  protocol at byte 9 and udpLen but never
                                                  inspects the flags/fragment-offset at
                                                  bytes 6-7. A non-initial fragment of
                                                  protocol 17 has arbitrary payload where
                                                  the UDP header is assumed; the udpLen
                                                  sanity check catches some but not all,
                                                  so a crafted fragment can be misread
                                                  into a fabricated forensic DNS record
                                                  while a legitimately fragmented large
                                                  answer is dropped. Most serious capture
                                                  item: fabricated/forgeable evidence.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Agree; Fix 1 (reject fragmented packets
                                                  with an explicit coverage caveat, or
                                                  bounded reassembly). Priority high.


                       **FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** IPv4 fragmented packets (MF=1 or fragment offset>0) are now explicitly rejected in parseIPUDPHeader; non-initial fragments can no longer be misread as complete UDP datagrams.
