                                                  macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/DNSCapture.swift:191-195;
                                                  Windows/SyxxCage/Program.cs:101-106;
                                                  Windows/Syxx.Kit/DNSCapture.cs:175-179 —
                                                  Live-source inspection confirms the cited concern
                                                  only in narrowed/current form: Although IPv4
                                                  validates UDP length, the returned context exposes
                                                  only an offset. Both callers slice from that
                                                  offset to the end of the captured buffer, not to
                                                  `ihl + udpLen`; `payloadBytes` then counts the
                                                  excess.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Keep buffer-tail defect; C029 is its
                                                  size-telemetry consequence and should
                                                  cross-reference/merge.

                       - **Tool Name**            [Claude]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       Confirmed. parseIPUDPHeader returns only
                                                  payloadOffset (ihl+8), not a validated
                                                  end (macOS DNSCapture.swift:262); the
                                                  caller SyxxCage.swift:232 slices
                                                  payloadOffset..<ipPayload.count (buffer
                                                  tail), and parseDNSPacket sets
                                                  payloadBytes: data.count (:355), so
                                                  link-layer padding/trailers inflate the
                                                  F9 size signal and any trailing bytes
                                                  are consumed as DNS tail. IPv4's earlier
                                                  udpLen validation is not applied to the
