                                                  failure case before closure.

                       - **Tool Name**            [Claude]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       Confirmed Program.cs:223 IOControl(ReceiveAll)
                                                  captures ALL IP; the :53 filter is userspace at
                                                  line 104 after the full read. macOS applies BPF
                                                  "udp port 53" at the kernel (SyxxCage.swift:117 /
                                                  Ccage.c:65-78). On a busy link the socket buffer
                                                  fills with non-DNS traffic -> backpressure can drop
                                                  real DNS packets (missed detection).
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Agree; Medium. [Fix 1] use a WFP/BPF-equivalent
                                                  kernel filter for UDP/53; [Fix 2] as a stopgap,
                                                  dedicate a reader thread with a larger buffer.
                                                  Priority: medium.

