- **[E038]**            **FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** Added `OptedOut` property (backed by `dimension_opt_out` settings key) and early-return guards in `FetchStartupAsync` and `FetchWhatsNewUrl`, matching macOS behavior. `RemoteContentPanel` handles null `SourceUrl` gracefully.
                        Windows DimensionService Lacks Opt-Out Check (Platform Parity)
- **Criticality:**      Non-critical (Medium); Windows users who have opted out of Dimension
                         telemetry are still contacted on every launch — the opt-out setting
                         exists only on macOS.
- **Location:**         Windows/SyxxUI/Services/DimensionService.cs:59-66;
                         macOS/Sources/SyxxApp/DimensionService.swift:51-53, 71-73, 86-88
- **Issue:**            [CONFIRMED] macOS DimensionService checks `UserDefaults.bool(forKey:
                         "dimension_opt_out")` at the top of `fetchStartup()` (line 51),
                         `fetchWhatsNewURL()` (line 71), and `fetchBroadcast()` (line 86),
                         returning nil/early when the user has opted out. Windows
                         `DimensionService.FetchStartupAsync()` (line 59-66) has no opt-out
                         check — it always fetches from the server. `FetchWhatsNewUrl()` (line
                         83-93) also has no check. The macOS AppModel exposes a
                         `dimensionOptIn` toggle (AppModel.swift:146-148) that writes the
                         UserDefaults key, but this setting has no effect on Windows because
                         the Windows DimensionService never reads it. A user who believes they
                         have opted out (via the macOS-equivalent UI toggle or profile
                         management) is silently contacted on Windows.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** Platform parity gap; no existing delta covers this specific omission.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Add an opt-out check (e.g., `ApplicationData.Current.LocalSettings`
                         key or a shared config flag) to `FetchStartupAsync()` and
                         `FetchWhatsNewUrl()`, matching the macOS behavior.
                         [Fix 2] Expose the opt-out toggle in the Windows UI (currently absent)
                         so the setting is actually reachable.
- **Code Sample:**      [

                         // Windows/SyxxUI/Services/DimensionService.cs:59-66 — no opt-out check
