- **[E040]**            **NON-CODEABLE** Binding multiple raw sockets per active interface requires substantial capture-loop redesign (concurrent socket management, per-interface attribution) — outside the scope of a minimal source fix.
                        Windows DNS Capture Single-Interface Binding Limitation — Cannot Capture on VPN or Multiple Interfaces
- **Criticality:**      Non-critical (High); fails to capture DNS traffic on active VPN tunnels or secondary interfaces.
- **Location:**         Windows/SyxxCage/Program.cs:207-218
- **Issue:**            [CONFIRMED] In the Windows raw socket sniffer setup, `OpenRawSocket` enumerates system IPs via `Dns.GetHostEntry(Dns.GetHostName())` and binds the socket to the first non-loopback IP address. On machines with multiple interfaces (e.g. WiFi and a VPN virtual adapter), it binds only to one arbitrary interface. Traffic going through the other interfaces (like a VPN tunnel) will be completely invisible to the capture, leading to missed DNS queries during VPN leak audits.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** E037 covers raw socket filtering, but interface selection limits are untracked.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Bind separate sockets to each active IP interface, or allow the user to select the interface via a command-line argument (similar to macOS BPF interface capture selection).
- **Code Sample:**      [

                        // Windows/SyxxCage/Program.cs:207-216
                        IPAddress bindAddress = family == AddressFamily.InterNetworkV6 ? IPAddress.IPv6Any : IPAddress.Any;
                        var host = Dns.GetHostEntry(Dns.GetHostName());
                        foreach (var ip in host.AddressList)
                        {
                            if (ip.AddressFamily == family && !IPAddress.IsLoopback(ip))
                            {
                                bindAddress = ip;
                                break;
                            }
                        }
                        // ^^ binds only to the first found non-loopback IP interface

                        ]
