                                                  installs context.coordinator and its URL/delegate
                                                  policy is immutable after initialization.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Archive; D033/D039 cover the actual permissive
                                                  navigation/resource policy.

                       - **Tool Name**            [Claude]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Disagree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       RemoteContentView.swift:32-37 — makeNSView
                                                  RE-attaches on the cached path (`cached.
                                                  navigationDelegate = context.coordinator`, :35),
                                                  and SwiftUI retains the coordinator for the
                                                  representable's lifetime and passes that same
                                                  instance to updateNSView, so there is no live
                                                  window where the delegate is nil under an in-tree
                                                  view; teardown+rebuild re-runs makeNSView which
