- **[A073]**            Server DNS Client Lacks EDNS0 Capability Support
- **Criticality:**      High; large responses containing DNSKEY/RRSIG data truncate, triggering TCP fallback.
- **Location:**         Server/syxx_server/resolver.py:55
- **Issue:**            [CONFIRMED] Outbound queries lack OPT records advertising larger UDP buffer support, limiting UDP payload limits and requiring TCP connections.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** SD-15 tracks the candidate; promoted here.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Include an EDNS0 OPT header in query packets.
- **Tag:**              CONFIRMED


                       - **Tool Name**            [Codex]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree with revisions
                       - **Disagree Basis**       _build_query emits no EDNS OPT record at
                                                  Server/syxx_server/resolver.py:55-60. TCP fallback
                                                  handles TC responses, so this is not blanket query
                                                  failure, but lack of DO/advertised payload impairs
                                                  DNSSEC observation and efficiency.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Merge the DNSSEC-critical portion with A030;
                                                  otherwise rate as compatibility/efficiency and
                                                  implement EDNS0 with bounded TCP fallback.

                       - **Tool Name**            [Claude]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree with revisions
                       - **Disagree Basis**       Confirmed: _build_query at resolver.py:55-60 packs
                                                  header with ARCOUNT=0 and emits no OPT record, so no
                                                  advertised UDP payload and no DO bit. TCP fallback
                                                  (:171-172,358-370) handles truncation, so this is
                                                  not a blanket failure. The mission-relevant edge:
                                                  without DO=1 many authoritatives omit RRSIG, so
                                                  investigate._dnssec_observed (which needs RRSIG,
                                                  investigate.py:120-130) can UNDER-report DNSSEC.
                                                  That is honest-inconclusive/underclaim, not a
                                                  false-secure, so criticality is compat/efficiency
                                                  plus DNSSEC-observation fidelity.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Implement EDNS0 OPT (payload ~1232, DO=1) with the
                                                  existing bounded TCP fallback; merge the
                                                  DNSSEC-observation portion with A030. Priority:
                                                  medium. Validation: query a signed zone (e.g.
                                                  cloudflare.com) and confirm RRSIG now appears where
                                                  it silently did not before.

**FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** `_build_query` (resolver.py) now always includes an EDNS0 OPT record advertising a 1232-byte UDP payload, reducing unnecessary TCP fallback. The DO bit is set only when explicitly requested via `do=True`.

