                                                  debunk.

**FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code), already resolved.** Python's `encode("idna")` has an ASCII fast-path that handles underscores correctly (`"_dmarc".encode("idna")` returns `b"_dmarc"`); no failing input exists. Claim debunked by both Codex and Claude reviewers.

