                                                  which automatically follows redirects. If a
                                                  captive portal redirects a query to a local login
                                                  page, the client downloads the full login resource
                                                  hierarchy, causing slowdowns and differing from
                                                  the Windows client which disables auto-redirects.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Keep in C-domain; required disposition: [Fix 1]
                                                  Configure the captive portal URLSession delegate
                                                  to reject redirects and evaluate the redirect
                                                  response code (302) directly as captive portal
                                                  presence.


