- **[B088]**            Dashboard “Trust Score” Reassures on Threat Verdicts
- **Criticality:**      Critical; a high-confidence threat can display as high trust on Windows,
                        while macOS invents trust as `100 - diagnosis confidence`.
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxApp/DashboardView.swift:239-250;
                        Windows/SyxxUI/Views/DashboardView.xaml.cs:31-33
- **Issue:**            Windows labels the conclusion confidence itself as TRUST SCORE regardless
                        of verdict, so 95%-confident tampering displays trust 95. macOS reverses the
                        number for every non-clean verdict, which can turn a low-confidence threat
                        into high green trust. Diagnostic confidence is not host trust and neither
                        arithmetic is valid. Archived GUIA-17 remains live.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** GUIA-17 in DELTAS-fixed.md; related color/output honesty findings B052-B053.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Display the typed verdict and its evidence confidence separately.
                        [Fix 2] Do not derive a trust score without a specified, tested model.
- **Tag:**              CONFIRMED — REOPENED REGRESSION


