- **[B089]**            Failed Manual Update Check Rebrands Stale Cache as Fresh “Up to Date”
- **Criticality:**      Critical; a blocked check can hide a newly released security update behind
                        a green fresh timestamp.
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxApp/DimensionService.swift:48-65;
                        macOS/Sources/SyxxApp/UpdatePanel.swift:155-167;
                        Windows/SyxxUI/Services/DimensionService.cs:59-78;
                        Windows/SyxxUI/Views/UpdatePanel.xaml.cs:51-76
- **Issue:**            Even `force: true` falls back to any cached startup response on network or
                        decode failure. Both panels then stamp “last checked” as now and map a stale
                        cached `available=false` to up-to-date. Response freshness/provenance is lost.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** D037 covers the cache’s missing authenticity, not this false-fresh verdict.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Return fresh/cache/error provenance and cache timestamp. [Fix 2]
                        A forced check failure must be unknown/failed; stale data may be labeled only
                        as “last known as of …”.
