- **[B091]**            **FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code), already resolved.** LeakDetector.swift:347-398 now derives the verdict exclusively from `extractSignedLeaked(from: result.signedPayload)` — the signed payload — not the unsigned outer `result.leaked`. Missing/malformed signed payload → `.inconclusive`. Invalid signature → `.inconclusive`. Untrusted signing key → `.inconclusive`. Leak Verdict Is Computed From Unsigned Outer Fields Instead of the Signed Payload
- **Criticality:**      Critical; a relay can preserve a valid signature while flipping the leak
                        verdict or resolver list shown by both clients.
- **Location:**         Server/syxx_server/leak.py:138-163;
                        macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/LeakDetector.swift:203-233,261-274;
                        Windows/Syxx.Kit/LeakDetector.cs:220-245,291-309
- **Issue:**            The server signs canonical `leaked` and `observedResolvers` inside
                        `signedPayload`, but clients reconcile verdict from separate outer response
                        properties. `verify()` checks only the signature over opaque payload bytes;
                        it never parses those bytes or proves equality with the outer fields. A
                        valid signed receipt can therefore accompany a forged outer verdict while
                        `signatureValid == true`.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** D004 covers invalid signatures not gating verdict; D011 covers unpinned keys.
                        Neither covers valid-signature/unsigned-field binding.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Parse a strict canonical signed-payload DTO after signature and key
                        validation. [Fix 2] Derive every verdict-bearing field exclusively from that
                        DTO and reject any duplicate outer-field mismatch.
- **Tag:**              CONFIRMED


                       - **Tool Name**            [Codex]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       Server/syxx_server/leak.py:138-163;
                                                  macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/LeakDetector.swift:203-233,261-274;
                                                  Windows/Syxx.Kit/LeakDetector.cs:220-245,291-309 —
                                                  Live-source inspection confirms the operative
                                                  behavior: The server signs canonical `leaked` and
                                                  `observedResolvers` inside `signedPayload`, but
                                                  clients reconcile verdict from separate outer
                                                  response properties. `verify()` checks only the
                                                  signature over opaque payload bytes; it never
                                                  parses those bytes or proves equality with the
                                                  outer fields. A valid signed receipt can therefore
                                                  accompany a forged outer verdict while
                                                  `signatureValid == true`.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Keep in B-domain; required disposition: [Fix 1]
                                                  Parse a strict canonical signed-payload DTO after
                                                  signature and key validation. [Fix 2] Derive every
                                                  verdict-bearing field exclusively from that DTO
                                                  and reject any duplicate outer-field mismatch.


                       - **Tool Name**            [Claude]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       Confirmed LeakDetector.cs:222-245 /
                                                  .swift:203-233 — verdict comes from
                                                  ReconcileVerdict(verifyResp.Leaked,
                                                  verifyResp.ObservedResolvers), the OUTER JSON
                                                  fields. Verify() (cs:291-310) only checks the
                                                  Ed25519 sig over the opaque SignedPayload base64
                                                  (leak.py:157-163); it never parses it or compares
                                                  it to the outer fields. A relay keeps sig +
                                                  SignedPayload intact, flips outer
                                                  leaked/observedResolvers → SignatureValid==true
                                                  beside a forged verdict. Codex correct.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Agree. Priority: Critical (forgeable evidence —
                                                  highest rank). Fixes 1+2 sound; strengthen: after
                                                  decoding the signed DTO, canonically re-serialize
                                                  it and byte-compare to the received SignedPayload
                                                  to defeat JSON-canonicalization ambiguity, and bind
                                                  the DTO keyId to the pinned trust set (D011) before
                                                  trusting any field.


                        - **Tool Name**            [opencode]
                        - **Date**                 2026-07-19
                        - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                        - **Disagree Basis**       N/A. Leak verdict computed from unsigned outer fields rather than signed payload. Verified: reconcileVerdict uses result.leaked unsigned.
                        - **Proposed Revisions**   Keep in B-domain; required disposition per Fix(es) above.

