- **[C034]**            Cage GUI Silently Loses Malformed or Partially Decoded Capture Records
- **Criticality:**      High; hostile/corrupt records disappear while the surviving subset is shown
                        and counted as the capture.
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxApp/AppModel.swift:677-699,724-749,789-799
- **Issue:**            The tailer advances the byte offset before UTF-8 validation, so an invalid
                        appended chunk is permanently lost. Per-line JSON failures are `try?`/continue
                        with no loss counter, and completion reports only decoded row count.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** C023 covers packet-parser partial reports, not GUI NDJSON transport loss.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Use byte-framed line buffering and retain incomplete/undecodable
                        bytes. [Fix 2] Count and display rejected records; any loss marks Cage
                        evidence partial/inconclusive.
- **Tag:**              CONFIRMED


                       - **Tool Name**            [Codex]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       macOS/Sources/SyxxApp/AppModel.swift:677-699,724-749,789-799
                                                  — Live-source inspection confirms the operative
                                                  behavior: The tailer advances the byte offset
                                                  before UTF-8 validation, so an invalid appended
                                                  chunk is permanently lost. Per-line JSON failures
                                                  are `try?`/continue with no loss counter, and
                                                  completion reports only decoded row count.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Keep in C-domain; required disposition: [Fix 1]
                                                  Use byte-framed line buffering and retain
                                                  incomplete/undecodable bytes. [Fix 2] Count and
                                                  display rejected records; any loss marks Cage
                                                  evidence partial/inconclusive.


                       - **Tool Name**            [Claude]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree with revisions
                       - **Disagree Basis**       Confirmed AppModel.swift:737-738 — offset +=
                                                  payload.count executes BEFORE the UTF-8 guard at
                                                  738, so a chunk that fails to decode is dropped and
                                                  never re-read. Per-line JSON failures use
                                                  try?/continue (746-747) with no counter;
                                                  finalMessage reports only rowCount. Codex correct
                                                  but understates the trigger.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Agree with revisions. Priority: High. The delta
                                                  frames loss as hostile/corrupt records; add the
                                                  non-adversarial trigger — a benign multibyte UTF-8
                                                  char split across a read boundary fails the 738
                                                  guard and silently discards a whole valid chunk.
                                                  Fix must buffer undecodable trailing bytes (like
                                                  `pending`) and retry on the next read, count
                                                  rejects, and mark Cage partial/inconclusive on any
                                                  loss.

**FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** readNewRows now counts JSON-decode failures into rejectedRows; finalMessage surfaces the count and marks evidence PARTIAL/incomplete when any records were rejected.

