                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       Server/syxx_server/dns_authoritative.py:40-99,175-190;
                                                  Server/syxx_server/leak.py:138-163 —
                                                  Production-source inspection shows: The parser
                                                  extracts TXID/QNAME/QTYPE but never requires QR=0,
                                                  opcode=QUERY, class=IN, or exactly one question.
                                                  The server records the UDP source before producing
                                                  a signed observed-resolver set. Anyone learning
                                                  the DNS-visible token can submit invalid
                                                  response-form packets; spoofable UDP source
                                                  further undermines attribution.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Retain the delta and its proposed fixes; require a
                                                  real production-path run and an adversarial or
                                                  failure case before closure.

                       - **Tool Name**            [Claude]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree with revisions
                       - **Disagree Basis**       Confirmed. _build_response (dns_authoritative.py:
                                                  40-99) validates only len>=12 and qd_count>=1; it
                                                  never checks QR=0 (reads only RD, line 61), opcode,
                                                  qclass==IN (qclass read at 52 then discarded), or
                                                  qdcount==1. _serve_dns:184-186 feeds addr[0] into
                                                  leak.observe, which writes it to the signed
                                                  observedResolvers set (verify() leak.py:145). Any
                                                  party who knows an issued token can inject
                                                  observations via response-form/multi-question/
                                                  wrong-class packets.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Agree on strict header validation + adversarial
                                                  tests, but add: it does NOT stop UDP source-IP
                                                  spoofing — a well-formed query with a forged source
                                                  still injects an arbitrary "resolver". The
                                                  attestation must explicitly caveat that
                                                  observedResolvers are unauthenticated UDP source IPs
                                                  (do not present spoofable data as authenticated
                                                  evidence). CRITICAL=Y (poisonable signed evidence).

