- **[F025]**            Windows Startup Dialog Race Can Permanently Lose a Critical Broadcast
- **Criticality:**      High; a critical MOTD can be marked dismissed even if it never appears.
- **Location:**         Windows/SyxxUI/MainWindow.xaml.cs:30-41,44-57,65-101
- **Issue:**            Broadcast and update dialogs are both fire-and-forget on the same XamlRoot;
                        when both are pending they race the one-dialog constraint. `DismissBroadcast`
                        is called immediately after invoking `ShowAsync`, before successful display
                        or user action, so a failed/competing dialog can be permanently suppressed.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** D032/D060 concern unsafe broadcast URLs, not delivery/dismissal integrity.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Await and serialize one dialog queue. [Fix 2] Persist dismissal only
                        after a completed explicit dismiss action; retain retry state on failure.
- **Tag:**              CONFIRMED source reachability; GUI reproduction still required


                       - **Tool Name**            [Codex]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       Windows/SyxxUI/MainWindow.xaml.cs:30-41,44-57,65-101
                                                  — Broadcast and update dialogs are both
                                                  fire-and-forget on the same XamlRoot; when both
                                                  are pending they race the one-dialog constraint.
                                                  `DismissBroadcast` is called immediately after
                                                  invoking `ShowAsync`, before successful display or
                                                  user action, so a failed/competing dialog can be
                                                  permanently suppressed.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Serialize dialogs and mark seen only after
                                                  display/acknowledgment.

                       - **Tool Name**            [Claude]
                       - **Date**                 2026-07-13
                       - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                       - **Disagree Basis**       Confirmed source. MainWindow.xaml.cs:100-101: `_ =
                                                  dialog.ShowAsync(); ViewModel.DismissBroadcast(
                                                  broadcast);` — dismissal is recorded immediately
                                                  after fire-and-forget ShowAsync, before display or
                                                  user action. Both broadcast (34) and update (40)
                                                  dialogs are fire-and-forget on the same XamlRoot;
                                                  WinUI allows one open ContentDialog, so the second
                                                  ShowAsync throws on an unobserved Task while
                                                  DismissBroadcast has already marked the MOTD seen.
                       - **Proposed Revisions**   Agree; MOTD delivery integrity, not verdict-
                                                  affecting, CRITICAL=N. Serialize a single dialog
                                                  queue, await each ShowAsync, and persist dismissal
                                                  only after a completed explicit dismiss (retain
                                                  retry state on failure/competition). GUI
                                                  reproduction still required for exact timing.

