- **[B145]**            **FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** `zone_signing_status` now iterates all three response sections (answers + authority + additional) for RRSIGs. `resolve_authoritative` now sets the DO bit (`do=True`) so authoritative queries include DNSSEC records.
- **Criticality:**      Medium; a signed zone with RRSIGs in non-answers sections reports uncertain DNSSEC
                        status, degrading the detection signal.
- **Location:**         Server/syxx_server/resolver.py:589-594
- **Issue:**            `_zone_is_signed` only iterates `resp["answers"]` for RRSIG records.
                        `_parse_sections` at resolver.py:497-501 parses all three sections (`answers`,
                        `authority`, `additional`), but `_zone_is_signed` only examines `answers`. Some
                        authoritative servers place RRSIGs in the additional section. A signed zone whose
                        DNSKEY+RRSIGs span sections returns `None` instead of `True`, degrading the
                        DNSSEC-based detection signal. Additionally, `_build_query` (resolver.py:84) does
                        not set the DO bit for regular queries, so the server is also systematically blind
                        to DNSSEC data when operators do not explicitly request it.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** B047 covers RRSIG validity span arithmetic. No existing delta covers missing
                        section scope or DO bit absence.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Iterate all three response sections for RRSIGs instead of only `answers`.
                        [Fix 2] Set the DO (DNSSEC OK) bit on authoritative queries so resolvers include
                        DNSSEC records.
                        [Fix 3] Add failure-case tests with RRSIGs in authority/additional sections.

- **Code Sample:**      [

                        # Server/syxx_server/resolver.py:589-594
                        for r in resp["answers"]:
                            if r.get("rtype") != TYPE_RRSIG:
                                continue
                            window = _parse_rrsig_window(r["value"], TYPE_DNSKEY)

                        ]


                        - **Tool Name**            [opencode]
                        - **Date**                 2026-07-19
                        - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                        - **Disagree Basis**       N/A. _zone_is_signed only checks answers section for RRSIGs, misses authority/additional. Verified: Server/syxx_server/resolver.py.
                        - **Proposed Revisions**   Keep in B-domain; required disposition per Fix(es) above.

