- **[B146]**            Windows `IsDNSEncrypted() => false` Stub Kills Sentinel Change Detection and
                        EncryptedDNSConfigurator
- **Criticality:**      Critical; the encrypted-DNS change-detection path and configurator are structurally
                        dead code on Windows.
- **Location:**         Windows/Syxx.Kit/NetworkKeyState.cs:383; Windows/Syxx.Kit/Trust.cs:159,173,223-225;
                        Windows/Syxx.Kit/EncryptedDNSConfigurator.cs:58-64
- **Issue:**            `IsDNSEncrypted()` at NetworkKeyState.cs:383 is hardcoded `=> false` with a comment
                        (lines 381-382) acknowledging it is a stub. This populates
                        `NetworkConfigSnapshot.DnsEncrypted` (Trust.cs:173), which `Sentinel.Diff` reads to
                        detect encrypted-DNS state changes. Since the value is always false, the diff
                        comparator can never detect a change — the entire `ConfigChangeKind.EncryptedDNSChanged`
                        detection path is dead code. Additionally, `EncryptedDNSConfigurator.EnableAsync` reads
                        this same stub; after a successful `netsh` DoH apply, `active` is always false, so
                        `ClassifyApply` produces at best `Inconclusive` — the configurator is structurally
                        incapable of returning `Enabled`.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** CHANGELOG CUR-002 notes the stub; no delta tracks the downstream consequences on
                        Sentinel and EncryptedDNSConfigurator.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Implement real Windows DoH detection via per-interface DohFlags registry or
                        `Get-DnsClientDohServerAddress`.
                        [Fix 2] Change `DnsEncrypted` to a tri-state so Unknown/Yes/No are distinguished.
                        [Fix 3] Remove the stub; the configurator should not pretend it can enable encrypted
                        DNS until detection is real.

- **Code Sample:**      [

                        // NetworkKeyState.cs:383
                        public static bool IsDNSEncrypted() => false;

                        ]


                        - **Tool Name**            [opencode]
                        - **Date**                 2026-07-19
                        - **Agree / Disagree**     Agree
                        - **Disagree Basis**       N/A. Windows IsDNSEncrypted() => false stub kills Sentinel change detection and EncryptedDNSConfigurator. Verified: hardcoded false.
                        - **Proposed Revisions**   Keep in B-domain; required disposition per Fix(es) above.


**FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code), already resolved.** IsDNSEncrypted() now delegates to EncryptedDNSStatus() which reads real system DoH/DoT state; stale comment cleaned up.
