- **[D074]**            **FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** `bundle-app.sh` `LSMinimumSystemVersion` changed from 13.0 to 14.0 to match `Package.swift` `.macOS(.v14)` and the actual `minos 14.0` in the bundled Mach-O executables.
                        macOS Bundle Advertises an Unsupported Deployment Floor
- **Criticality:**      High distribution defect. LaunchServices can offer the app to a system whose
                        executable cannot load.
- **Location:**         macOS/bundle-app.sh:29-46; macOS/Package.swift:4-8; MEMORY.md:283-284
- **Issue:**            CODE DEFECT. The generated Info.plist advertises macOS 13, SwiftPM requires
                        macOS 14, and both bundled Mach-O executables report `minos 14.0`. Project memory
                        separately states macOS 26 as the required target. These three incompatible
                        contracts make compatibility claims unreliable. On macOS 13, discovery/install
                        can appear supported even though the executable cannot run.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** No active/fixed/rejected delta records this metadata/executable mismatch.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Establish one approved minimum deployment target and derive SwiftPM,
                        Info.plist, and build settings from it.
                        [Fix 2] Gate packaging by comparing `vtool` minimum OS for every executable to
                        `LSMinimumSystemVersion` and failing on disagreement.
- **Code Sample:**      [

                        # bundle-app.sh:46 versus Package.swift:7
                        <key>LSMinimumSystemVersion</key><string>13.0</string>
                        .macOS(.v14)

                        ]
