**Issue:** When the token API call fails or returns non-2xx, `apiOk` stays `false` and the page **fabricates its own subdomains** (`hexToken() + '.leaktest.syxx.app'`) and then runs the full measurement theatre against them: the progress bar animates to 100%, and the step label prints `Resolving 3 of 6: <fabricated FQDN>` — a user-visible claim that a specific DNS lookup was performed and observed, when no token was ever registered server-side and nothing can possibly be recorded. This is a mock rendering as a measurement (honesty spine #4). The in-source comment at line 198 concedes the probes "will likely fail for mock subdomains, which is fine" — it is not fine; the UI does not distinguish it from a real run.

