**[A191]**
**Criticality:** HIGH
**Location:** `Server/leak-test.html:150-153` vs `Server/leaktest.html:263-274`
**Issue:** The two shipped leak-test pages answer the **same question from the same measurement with contradictory thresholds and contradictory certainty**. For an observation of exactly **2 unique resolvers**, `leak-test.html:151` renders green `v-safe` / **"No leak detected"**, while `leaktest.html:270-271` renders amber `warn` / "2 different resolvers observed your DNS queries" with the explicit caveat "This test cannot determine whether this is a leak." For **1 resolver**, `leak-test.html` asserts "your VPN or configured resolver appears to be handling all lookups" while `leaktest.html:268` states the opposite epistemic position: "This test cannot confirm whether your DNS traffic is encrypted or whether this resolver is the one you intended to use." Two pages served from the same origin disagreeing about one measurement is a defect independent of which one is right — and here the un-hedged page is the wrong one. Both are reachable: `leaktest` is served by Host-based routing at `Server/syxx_server/app.py:717-718`, and both filenames sit in the served web root.
**Cross-ref. Delta:** No delta ID matches. The C076 hedging was applied to exactly one of two pages; the divergence is untracked. **NEW — file a delta.**
**Fix(es):**
1. Collapse to one page. Two files (`leaktest.html`, `leak-test.html`) implementing one product surface with two different APIs (`/api/leaktest/*` vs `/api/leak/*`) and two different verdict tables is a maintenance trap that has already produced a doctrine violation.
2. If both must remain, extract the verdict logic to a single shared `leak-verdict.js` so a wording/threshold change cannot land on one page only, and make the C076 hedge the single source of truth.
3. Add a test asserting that no leak-test surface emits a string matching `/no (dns )?leak detected/i` or `/leak detected/i` — a golden-vector-style guard on the wording, since this is the exact class of regression C076 was raised for.
**Code Sample:**
`leak-test.html` — 2 resolvers is green/safe:
```
151	  if (count <= 2) setVerdict('v-safe', 'No leak detected', `Your DNS queries resolved through ${count} resolver${count===1?'':'s'}. Your VPN or configured resolver appears to be handling all lookups.`);
```
`leaktest.html` — 2 resolvers is amber/warn and explicitly refuses a verdict:
```
