- **[A216]**           Two Honesty Guards Registered in the Coverage Gate Live in Classes Defined
                        AFTER `if __name__ == "__main__"` — Invisible Under the Invocation Their Own
                        Docstrings Prescribe
- **Criticality:**      High (the A024 / A009 / A023 guards are the exact three the 2026-07-16 audit
                        found deletable against a green suite).
- **Location:**         Server/tests/test_leak.py:115-116 (`__main__`) vs 119-168 (`LeakHonestyGuardTests`);
                        Server/tests/test_dimension.py:127-128 (`__main__`) vs 131-157
                        (`PassiveDNSPIIBoundaryTests`)
- **Issue:**            `unittest.main()` runs at module level. In `test_leak.py` it sits at line 116,
                        while `LeakHonestyGuardTests` — which holds
                        `test_empty_collector_is_inconclusive_and_UNSIGNED` (A024, the refusal to sign
                        a clean verdict on zero observations) and `test_never_issued_token_writes_nothing`
                        (A009) — is not defined until line 119. Under
                        `python3 tests/test_leak.py`, `unittest.main()` discovers only the classes bound
                        at that instant: `LeakAttestationTests`. The two honesty guards never run and
                        the process exits 0. Identically in `test_dimension.py`: `PassiveDNSPIIBoundaryTests`
                        (A023, the resolver-IP PII strip) is defined 4 lines after `unittest.main()`.
                        Both files' docstrings direct the reader to exactly that invocation —
                        test_leak.py:11 "Run from Server/: python3 -m unittest tests.test_leak -v",
                        test_dimension.py:4 the same. (The `-m unittest tests.X` form imports the module
                        rather than running it as `__main__`, so it is safe; a bare
                        `python3 tests/test_leak.py`, which is what a hurried operator types, is not.)
                        Under pytest — the CI path — all classes are collected, so this is currently
                        latent rather than live. It is still a booby trap of the exact shape being
                        hunted: an appended class is a class the file's own documented entry point
                        silently drops, and the three guards it drops are the three the honesty gate
                        exists to protect.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** A024 / A009 / A023 — all three are registered in
                        scripts/honesty-coverage-gate.py:52-72. The gate runs the suite under pytest,
                        so it does not detect this.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Move the `if __name__ == "__main__": unittest.main()` block to the end
                        of both files (it is a one-line move; the classes are already correct).
                        [Fix 2] Add a suite-level meta-test that asserts no class is defined after the
                        `__main__` guard in any `tests/*.py` — this is mechanically checkable with `ast`
                        and would have caught both.

