- **[B208]**           **FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code), already resolved.** macOS MatrixDeterminativeEngine.swift:860 already uses `continue` (not `break`) when the missing-section flag is off, with B166 comment. C# twin still needs the fix.
                        Required-Section Gate Loop `break`s Out of the Whole Loop When
                        `HardGateOnMissingRequiredSections` Is False — Remaining Required Sections
                        Are Never Checked (shared with macOS)
- **Criticality:**      Low (dormant: the shipped spec sets the flag `true`,
                        `SyxxMatrixIntegration.cs:362`). Reported because it is a fail-open shape
                        in the gate that the honesty contract calls fail-closed.
- **Location:**         `MatrixDeterminativeEngine.cs:968-978` (the `break` at `:977` sits outside
                        the `if` at `:972` but inside the `TryGetValue` failure branch); identical
                        in `MatrixDeterminativeEngine.swift:796-803`.
- **Issue:**            With the flag off, a diagnosis whose FIRST required section is absent
                        `break`s the loop, so a SECOND required section that is present-but-
                        `Invalidated` (which would gate regardless of that flag, per
                        `FailClosedOnInvalidatedRequiredSections`) is never examined. The flags are
                        independent by design, so one flag being off should not disable the other.
                        Not a parity defect — both platforms share it — but it is a latent
                        fail-open in the gate.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** None found.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] `continue` instead of `break` when the missing-section flag is off;
                        `break` only when a gate is actually set. Apply to both platforms in the
                        same pass. [Fix 2] Golden vector with the flag off, requiring
                        `[missingSection, invalidatedSection]`, asserting the invalidated gate
                        still fires.
- **Code Sample:**      [

                        // MatrixDeterminativeEngine.cs:970-978
                        if (!sectionById.TryGetValue(reqSection, out var section))
                        {
                            if (Spec.Thresholds.HardGateOnMissingRequiredSections) { r.Gate = new GateInfo(…); }
                            break;   // exits even when no gate was set
                        }

                        ]

