**Criticality:** MEDIUM
**Location:** `scripts/win-build.ps1:16-19, 27-29, 48`
**Issue:** A stale duplicate of the repo-root `build.ps1` that cannot run. Every project path is
missing the `dotNET\` segment introduced when the tree was reorganised — `Windows\SyxxUI\SyxxUI.csproj`
instead of `Windows\dotNET\SyxxUI\SyxxUI.csproj` — so the first `dotnet build` fails with
MSB1009 and the script exits 1 (line 32-33). It also names its parameter `$args` (line 27),
shadowing PowerShell's automatic `$args` variable, and then splats it (`dotnet build @args`,
line 29); the root `build.ps1` already renamed this to `$buildArgs` (build.ps1:27, 30), which is the
tell that this file is an un-migrated copy. Line 48 additionally prints a `bin\Release\...\$plat\`
path with the configuration and platform segments transposed relative to the actual output layout
used by `ci.yml:178` (`bin/` under `SyxxUI`) and `build.ps1:48`.
**Cross-ref. Delta:** none — new.
**Fix(es):** delete `scripts/win-build.ps1` — `build.ps1` at the repo root is the corrected version
and having two divergent copies is how the stale one gets run. If it must stay, make it a
one-line delegation to `build.ps1`.
**Code Sample:**
```powershell
# scripts/win-build.ps1:16-19 — paths that no longer exist
$gui  = "Windows\SyxxUI\SyxxUI.csproj"
$kit  = "Windows\Syxx.Kit\Syxx.Kit.csproj"
$cli  = "Windows\Syxx\Syxx.csproj"
$test = "Windows\Syxx.Tests\Syxx.Tests.csproj"
