**[E058]**
**FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** Added SyxxUI.Avalonia.csproj and SyxxUI.Avalonia.Tests.csproj to Windows/Syxx.Linux.slnf; CI already has a dedicated linux-gui job.
**Criticality:** CRITICAL
**Location:** `Ubuntu/SyxxUI.Avalonia.Tests/`, `Windows/Syxx.Linux.slnf:4-8`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml:74,100,106`
**Issue:** **Nothing in CI ever compiles the Linux GUI.** The Linux solution filter contains
only `Syxx.Kit`, `Syxx` (CLI) and `Syxx.Tests`. `Ubuntu/SyxxUI.Avalonia` and
`Ubuntu/SyxxUI.Avalonia.Tests` appear **zero times** in `.github/` (verified by grep). The
Avalonia project links shared honesty code by path
(`..\..\Windows\dotNET\SyxxUI\Services\DimensionService.cs`) and references `Syxx.Kit`
directly, so any Kit or `DimensionService` change can break the *first platform to ship* with a
fully green CI. `WitnessTestifyParityTests.cs` — a parity test for the honesty surface — has
never been executed by any automated job. This is the same hole `ci.yml:88-98` documents and
fixes for the *Windows* GUI, left open for the platform that ships first.
**Cross-ref. Delta:** analogous to D101 (SyxxUI.Tests first-compile), not yet raised for Linux.
**Fix(es):** add `Ubuntu/SyxxUI.Avalonia/SyxxUI.Avalonia.csproj` and
`Ubuntu/SyxxUI.Avalonia.Tests/SyxxUI.Avalonia.Tests.csproj` to `Syxx.Linux.slnf` (paths are
relative to `Windows/Syxx.sln`, so `..\Ubuntu\...`), or add explicit `dotnet build` +
`dotnet test` steps guarded by `runner.os == 'Linux'`.
**Code Sample:**
```json
// Windows/Syxx.Linux.slnf:4-8 — the GUI that ships first is absent
    "projects": [
      "dotNET\\Syxx.Kit\\Syxx.Kit.csproj",
      "dotNET\\Syxx\\Syxx.csproj",
      "dotNET\\Syxx.Tests\\Syxx.Tests.csproj"
    ]
```

