**[E061]**
**FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** Git-added Linux/snap/snapcraft.yaml, Linux/Ubuntu/build_deb.sh, and Avalonia source files to the repository.
**Criticality:** HIGH
**Location:** `Linux/snap/snapcraft.yaml` (whole file), `Ubuntu/build_deb.sh` (whole file)
**Issue:** Both packaging inputs for the first-ship platform are **untracked in git**
(`git status --porcelain` reports `?? Linux/` and `?? Ubuntu/build_deb.sh`; `git ls-files
Linux/` is empty; `git check-ignore` returns rc=1, so they are not deliberately ignored — just
never added). Consequences: no CI can ever see them, no review, and a clean clone of the repo
cannot produce the shipping artifact. `git log -- Linux/snap/snapcraft.yaml` is empty, so
defects L2-01 through L2-03 have never passed through a diff.
**Cross-ref. Delta:** none — new.
**Fix(es):** `git add Linux/snap/snapcraft.yaml Ubuntu/build_deb.sh` (explicit paths only, per
lane rules) and add a `snapcraft --destructive-mode` build leg to `ci.yml`.

