**[E065]**
**FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** Added all missing hardening directives: `RestrictAddressFamilies`, `SystemCallFilter`, `SystemCallArchitectures`, `MemoryDenyWriteExecute`, `ProtectKernelTunables/Modules/Logs`, `ProtectControlGroups`, `ProtectClock`, `ProtectProc`, `RestrictNamespaces/SUIDSGID/Realtime`, `LockPersonality`, `PrivateUsers`, `UMask=0077`, `StartLimitIntervalSec=300`, `StartLimitBurst=5`.
**Criticality:** HIGH
**Location:** `scripts/deploy.sh:312-363`
**Issue:** `syxx-server.service` hardening is a partial set. Present: `NoNewPrivileges`,
`ProtectSystem=strict`, `ProtectHome`, `PrivateDevices`, `PrivateTmp`,
`AmbientCapabilities`/`CapabilityBoundingSet` scoped to `CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE`.
**Missing entirely**, for a daemon whose whole job is parsing hostile DNS packets on :53:
`RestrictAddressFamilies=AF_INET AF_INET6 AF_UNIX`, `SystemCallFilter=@system-service`,
`SystemCallArchitectures=native`, `MemoryDenyWriteExecute`, `ProtectKernelTunables`,
`ProtectKernelModules`, `ProtectKernelLogs`, `ProtectControlGroups`, `ProtectClock`,
`ProtectProc=invisible`, `RestrictNamespaces`, `RestrictSUIDSGID`, `RestrictRealtime`,
`LockPersonality`, `PrivateUsers`, `UMask=0077`. Also absent: `StartLimitIntervalSec` /
`StartLimitBurst` alongside `Restart=always`+`RestartSec=5` (line 322-323), which SD-56
explicitly asked for and which still allows an infinite crash loop on a config error. No UFW,
no fail2ban and no `unattended-upgrades` anywhere in the script (`grep -i 'ufw|fail2ban|
firewall|StartLimit'` → no matches), the other three SD-56 legs.
**Cross-ref. Delta:** SD-56 (`Server/SERVER_DELTAS.md:135`) — three of four legs still open.
**Fix(es):** add the directives above; validate with `systemd-analyze security syxx-server`
and record the score in the deploy output so a regression is visible.
**Code Sample:**
```ini
# scripts/deploy.sh:348-359 — the entire hardening block as shipped
AmbientCapabilities=CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE
CapabilityBoundingSet=CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE
NoNewPrivileges=true
ProtectSystem=strict
ReadWritePaths=${REMOTE_DIR}
ProtectHome=true
PrivateDevices=true
PrivateTmp=true
```

