**[E086]**
**Criticality:** CRITICAL (systemic) — the entire shipped Linux surface has zero tests, and the
Linux test project tests the GUI instead
**Location:** `Windows/dotNET/Syxx.Tests/Syxx.Tests.csproj:15-17`,
`Ubuntu/SyxxUI.Avalonia.Tests/` (2 files, 383 lines, 6 `[Fact]`s), `Windows/Syxx.Linux.slnf`,
`.github/workflows/ci.yml:74-115`
**Issue:** Three separate holes that compound.

1. **No test project references the CLI.** `Syxx.Tests.csproj` declares exactly two
   `ProjectReference`s — `Syxx.Kit` and `Syxx.Telemetry`. It does **not** reference
   `Windows/dotNET/Syxx/Syxx.csproj`. A grep across `Windows/dotNET/Syxx.Tests/` and
   `Ubuntu/SyxxUI.Avalonia.Tests/` for `Syxx.Commands|CageCommand|LeakCommand|WitnessCommand|
   RouteCommand|NslookCommand|FirstRunCommand|Program` returns **zero hits**. So `Program.cs`
   (1003 lines) plus 16 command files — the whole thing the snap ships — are covered by **0 of the
   165 `[Fact]`/`[Theory]` cases** in the suite. Every defect in [L4-02] through [L4-14] lives in
   code no test can even see.

2. **`Ubuntu/SyxxUI.Avalonia.Tests` tests nothing Linux-specific.** Its 6 tests are
   `WitnessViewModelTests` (5, all `SignAsync_*` on the Avalonia Witness view-model) and
   `WitnessTestifyParityTests` (2, fixture parity). Zero tests touch path handling, `~/.syxx`
   permissions, secret storage, resolver detection, capture capability, distro detection, or exit
   codes. The csproj comment even scopes it out: *"Only ViewModel-level logic is exercised here"*.
   The one Linux-named test file in the repo, `Windows/dotNET/Syxx.Tests/LinuxDistroTests.cs`,
   feeds `/etc/os-release` **string literals** to a pure parser — it never reads a file, never
   touches a filesystem, and proves nothing about behaviour on a Linux host. `OTelBootstrapTests.cs:77`
   (`if (OperatingSystem.IsLinux()) Assert.Equal("linux", os);`) is the sum total of behaviour that
   is actually asserted differently on Linux.

3. **CI never runs `Ubuntu/SyxxUI.Avalonia.Tests`, never packages, and proves only that things
   compile.** `grep -n Avalonia .github/workflows/ci.yml` → no hits. `grep -n 'snap\|build_deb\|\.deb'`
   → no hits. The Linux legs (`ci.yml:74-76`, `:100-102`, `:107-115`) do
   `dotnet build Windows/Syxx.Linux.slnf`, `dotnet test Syxx.Tests`, and
   `dotnet publish Syxx.csproj -r linux-{x64,arm64} --self-contained`. That publish step is
   explicitly labelled "Real-run bar" in the comment at `:104-105` — but a successful `publish` is
   not a run. It is exactly what let [L4-01]'s indexed `FileName = "tracert"` and [L4-04]'s
   SIO_RCVALL sit in the ship-first artifact: both compile perfectly.

Net effect: on the platform that ships first, the shipped binary is never executed by any automated
process, and its only "Linux" tests are string-parsing unit tests and a GUI view-model suite that
CI does not invoke. Doctrine #5 — "the bar is a real run with honest output, not green tests" —
is not met on Linux by anything in the repository.
**Cross-ref. Delta:** none — new. Sibling L2-08 covers the missing snap-build leg; this is the
missing *execution* leg and the missing CLI test project.
**Fix(es):**
- Add `Syxx.CLI.Tests` referencing `Syxx.csproj`, and refactor `Main` to
  `Task<int> RunAsync(string[] args, TextWriter output)` so subcommand output and exit codes are
  assertable ([L4-02] makes this necessary anyway).
- Add Linux-behaviour tests that are skipped elsewhere (`[SkippableFact]` on
  `OperatingSystem.IsLinux()`): `~/.syxx` and `captures/` mode is 0700 ([L4-06], [L4-07]);
  `GetScopedResolversFromResolvectl` against a captured `resolvectl status` fixture **and** against
  a host with `resolvectl` absent; `syxx cage` on a box without CAP_NET_RAW yields UNTESTED and a
  non-zero exit ([L4-04]); `syxx lan` on a box without `net-tools` yields partial, not empty
  ([L4-14]).
- Add a CI leg on `ubuntu-latest` and `ubuntu-24.04-arm` that **runs the published binary**:
  `./out/$RID/Syxx --version`, `./out/$RID/Syxx --help`, `./out/$RID/Syxx route 8.8.8.8`,
  `./out/$RID/Syxx cage --duration 1`, `echo | ./out/$RID/Syxx` with a timeout ([L4-09]), asserting
  on both stdout content and `$?`.
- Wire `dotnet test Ubuntu/SyxxUI.Avalonia.Tests` into the Linux legs so its 6 tests at least run.
**Code Sample:**
```xml
<!-- Windows/dotNET/Syxx.Tests/Syxx.Tests.csproj:14-17 — the CLI is not referenced, so it is not testable -->
<ItemGroup>
  <ProjectReference Include="..\Syxx.Kit\Syxx.Kit.csproj" />
  <ProjectReference Include="..\Syxx.Telemetry\Syxx.Telemetry.csproj" />
</ItemGroup>
```
```yaml
# .github/workflows/ci.yml:104-115 — "Real-run bar" that never runs anything
# Real-run bar: the CLI must self-contained-publish for each Linux RID with its
# per-RID libsodium.so. Untrimmed on purpose (NSec + DNS reflection are trim-hostile).
- name: Verify self-contained CLI publish (${{ matrix.rid }})
  if: matrix.kind == 'dotnet' && runner.os == 'Linux'
  run: >
    dotnet publish Windows/dotNET/Syxx/Syxx.csproj -c Release
    -r ${{ matrix.rid }} --self-contained true -p:PublishSingleFile=true
    -o out/${{ matrix.rid }}
# (no step ever executes out/${{ matrix.rid }}/Syxx)
```

