- **Issue:**            The line is a literal. On a fresh launch the ring beside it reads "0 of 6"
                        (:56) while this sentence says four wardens are keeping watch. The clause
                        "the encrypted road stays sealed" asserts DNS encryption unconditionally,
                        including when `model.isEncrypted` is false — the pill two lines up
                        (:65, :430-432) will simultaneously read "Do53 · clear". Three surfaces in
                        one card, two of them live, one of them a decorative lie that overrides the
                        others in plain English.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** Family of F017 (DELTAS.md:11012, "ProphetView Hardcoded 'Interface en0 •
                        Wi-Fi • assigned by DHCP' Presented as Fact") and F016 (DELTAS.md:10973).
                        No open delta cites this string. NEW.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Derive from state: "\(completedWardens) of 6 checks have run" +
                        a separate honest transport clause driven by `cachedEncryptedDNSStatus`
                        (tri-state: encrypted / not encrypted / not determined).
                        [Fix 2] If lore copy is required, make it state-independent — lore must never
                        contain a count or a security claim.
- **FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** Hardcoded banner replaced with dynamic "\(completedWardens) of 6 checks have run." plus state-driven encryption clause.
- **Code Sample:**      [

                        // DashboardView.swift:96
                        Text("Four wardens keep watch; two await your call — the encrypted road stays sealed.")

                        ]

