- **[E095]**               DashboardView "Enable Encrypted DNS" Tile Is Dead UI Permanently Asserting
                        "Disabled — traffic already encrypted (VPN)"
- **Criticality:**      Non-critical (High); a non-interactive tile tells every user their traffic is
                        already encrypted through a VPN, measured or not.
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxApp/DashboardView.swift:199-223
- **Issue:**            Unlike its two siblings (:143 `flushDNSCache`, :171 `setUnbound`) this is a
                        bare `HStack`, not a `Button` — there is no action, no gate, and no path by
                        which a user can enable encrypted DNS from the Dashboard. It is dimmed to
                        `.opacity(0.5)` (:220) and captioned with the literal "Disabled — traffic
                        already encrypted (VPN)" (:210), plus an accessibility hint that repeats the
                        claim verbatim to VoiceOver users (:223: "DNS encryption is disabled because
                        your traffic is already encrypted through a VPN").

                        Nothing consults `model.portalReport?.vpn.state` — which is a genuine
                        tri-state (`.yes`/`.no`/`.unknown`, rendered honestly in PortalView
                        :136-143 and GluttonView :96-104). With no VPN and no encryption the user is
                        told, in two places including assistive technology, that they are protected.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** Family of F016/F017 (hardcoded state as fact, DELTAS.md:10973, :11012).
                        Dead-control aspect is untracked. NEW.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Make it a real `Button` routed to `SettingsView`'s working
                        `EncryptedDNSConfigurator` path (SettingsView.swift:164-192), which already
                        renders the honest five-state result.
                        [Fix 2] Until then, drive the caption and the disabled state from
                        `portalReport?.vpn.state` + `cachedEncryptedDNSStatus`, with "not determined"
                        as the default — never "already encrypted".
                        [Fix 3] Fix the accessibility hint; it currently states the claim as fact.
- **FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** Tile caption, opacity, and accessibility hint now driven by cachedEncryptedDNSStatus tri-state; no longer asserts VPN encryption unconditionally.
- **Code Sample:**      [

                        // DashboardView.swift:199-223 — no Button, no state read
                        HStack(spacing: 10) {
                            ...
                            Text("Enable Encrypted DNS")
                            Text("Disabled — traffic already encrypted (VPN)")
                        }
                        .opacity(0.5)
                        .accessibilityHint("DNS encryption is disabled because your traffic is already encrypted through a VPN")

                        ]

