- **[E107]**               ConclusionsView Glutton Evidence Row States an Observation Count Without the
                        Verdict That Qualifies It
- **Criticality:**      Non-critical (Med); "Collector observed 0 resolver IP(s)" reads as a clean
                        measurement when the collector may have errored or been unreachable.
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxApp/ConclusionsView.swift:202-204
- **Issue:**            The row prints `leak.observedResolvers.count` and `transportPinning`, but not
                        `leak.verdict`. `LeakVerdict` distinguishes `.notDetected` ("the collector
                        observed queries and confirmed none reached an unexpected resolver"),
                        `.inconclusive`, `.invalid`, and `.error` (LeakDetector.swift:21-31). All
                        four can yield an empty `observedResolvers`, and all four render the same
                        sentence. `transportPinning == .failed` — which LeakDetector documents as
                        forcing the verdict to inconclusive (:56-59) — is shown only as a raw enum
                        name with no qualification.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** Adjacent to B066 (DELTAS.md:11926) and D011. NEW.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Lead the row with `leak.verdict`, then the count as its supporting
                        detail. [Fix 2] When `transportPinning == .failed`, state plainly that the
                        collector's identity could not be verified and the count is not evidence.
- **Code Sample:**      [

                        // ConclusionsView.swift:203
                        evidenceRow(title: "Glutton", fact: "Collector observed \(leak.observedResolvers.count) resolver IP(s) during probe. Transport status: \(leak.transportPinning.rawValue).")

                        ]
- **FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** Glutton evidence row now leads with result, states transport verification failure plainly when failed.

---
---

- **[E108]**               ProphetView `@State localDomain` Shadows `model.domain` and Clobbers It With
                        an Empty String
- **Criticality:**      Non-critical (Med); view-local state overwrites shared model state, and the
                        result card then names the wrong (or an empty) domain.
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxApp/ProphetView.swift:6, 53, 64-66, 128
- **Issue:**            `localDomain` is initialised to `""` and never seeded from `model.domain`, so
                        arriving at Prophet after typing a domain in Mirror/Portal/Witness (all of
                        which bind `$model.domain` directly) shows an empty field. Pressing "Divine
                        the address" assigns `model.domain = localDomain` **unconditionally** —
                        including the empty string — then calls `model.run()`. That silently erases a
                        domain the user entered in another pane, for every other pane.
                        The result card at :128 interpolates `model.domain`, so after an empty-field
                        press it reads "N oracles were queried for  ; all returned the same
                        address". No guard exists on the button (compare MirrorView.swift:65,
                        `.disabled(model.isRunning)`, which at least gates concurrency).
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** Adjacent to DELTAS.md:6091 ("affects ProphetView, PortalView, WitnessView,
                        and any view with TextField"). Not tracked for the clobber/shadow. NEW.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Bind the TextField to `$model.domain` as every other pane does, or
                        seed `localDomain` in `.onAppear` and write back only when non-empty.
                        [Fix 2] Disable the run button on an empty/whitespace domain.
- **Code Sample:**      [

                        // ProphetView.swift:6
                        @State private var localDomain: String = ""
                        // ProphetView.swift:64-66
                        Button(action: {
                            model.domain = localDomain
                            model.run()
                        })

                        ]
- **FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** Removed localDomain shadow, bind directly to $model.domain, disable button on empty/whitespace domain.

