---

- **[E109]**               ProphetView Result Card Is Unconditionally Success-Tinted
- **Criticality:**      Non-critical (Med); card fill, border, glowing dot and both text colours are
                        the same teal whatever the result.
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxApp/ProphetView.swift:118-126, 155-168
- **Issue:**            `tealColor` (`#2dd4bf`, the same value as `.ioSuccessGreen` dark variant —
                        IoDesignSystem.swift:39) is applied to: the status dot with a glow shadow
                        (:119-122), the verdict headline (:125), the consensus value (:162), the card
                        background at 5% (:166) and its border at 24% (:168). Even the honest
                        single-resolver branch ("Only one resolver queried; no consensus possible",
                        :123) — a genuinely inconclusive state — is rendered in success-teal with a
                        glowing green dot. There is no code path in this view that renders Prophet in
                        any non-reassuring colour.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** F018 (DELTAS.md:11051, "ProphetView DNSSEC .inconclusive Rendered
                        Critical-Red — Unmeasured State") is the inverse defect at the same view;
                        that surface is gone and this one replaced it. NEW.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Derive the accent from the result state via `Color.ioSeverity`.
                        [Fix 2] The `<2 resolvers` branch must render `.ioInfoPurple` (inconclusive),
                        matching `OverallVerdictView.stateColor` (:281-282).
- **Code Sample:**      [

                        // ProphetView.swift:119-125
                        Circle().fill(tealColor).shadow(color: tealColor, radius: 8)
                        Text(result.consensus.resolversQueried >= 2 ? "No tampering — resolvers agree" : "Only one resolver queried; no consensus possible")
                            .foregroundColor(tealColor)
                        // ProphetView.swift:166-168
                        .background(tealColor.opacity(0.05))
                        .overlay(RoundedRectangle(cornerRadius: 14).stroke(tealColor.opacity(0.24), lineWidth: 1))

                        ]
- **FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code), already resolved.** ProphetView now has evaluateConsensus() with proper ResolverConsensus states (.inconclusive, .insufficient, .agree, .disagree) and ConsensusPresentation that derives colors from state (ioSuccessGreen for agree, ioWarningAmber for disagree, ioTextSecondary for inconclusive/insufficient).

