---

- **[E115]**               SettingsView Encrypted-DNS Toggle Stays ON When the System Refused the Change
- **Criticality:**      Non-critical (Med); the switch position contradicts the honest text beneath
                        it, and the switch is the louder signal.
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxApp/SettingsView.swift:44-47, 63, 164-172, 179-192
- **Issue:**            `applyEncryption` is fire-and-forget from `onChange` (:46). On
                        `.entitlementRequired` (this build cannot change system DNS) or
                        `.failed(reason)` (DNS left unchanged), `settings.encryptedDNSEnabled`
                        remains `true` and the toggle stays in the ON position; only the caption at
                        :63 tells the truth. `describe()` (:179-192) is genuinely exemplary —
                        five honest states including "Treated as NOT protected until confirmed" —
                        but a user scanning the pane sees a switch that reads "encryption on".
                        The file's own header comment (:7-10) states the intent: "a toggle records
                        intent; it never asserts a capability is in effect" — the control's visual
                        affordance does assert it.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** Not tracked. NEW.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Revert the toggle to OFF on `.entitlementRequired` / `.failed`,
                        keeping the explanatory text.
                        [Fix 2] Or render a separate "in effect / not in effect" status pill next to
                        the toggle so intent and effect are visually distinct.
- **Code Sample:**      [

                        // SettingsView.swift:44-47
                        Toggle("Encrypt all DNS queries", isOn: $settings.encryptedDNSEnabled)
                            .onChange(of: settings.encryptedDNSEnabled) { _, on in
                                persist(); Task { await applyEncryption(on) }
                            }

                        ]
- **FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code), already resolved.** applyEncryption() now accepts priorValue and reverts settings.encryptedDNSEnabled to priorValue on .entitlementRequired, .failed, or .inconclusive results. Toggle only persists as ON when the system actually accepted the change.

---
---

- **[E116]**               SettingsView Asserts "Not enabled." Before Any Measurement
- **Criticality:**      Non-critical (Low); an unmeasured state rendered as a determinate one. Errs
