## Surfaces verified CORRECT (no finding — recorded so a later pass does not re-litigate)

- `PortalView.swift:189-225` — traceroute renders a genuine five-state machine, and `.failed`
  explicitly says "This is not evidence of a clean path." (:208). Exemplary.
- `PortalView.swift:136-143`, `GluttonView.swift:96-104` — VPN `.unknown` rendered amber and labelled
  "Unknown", distinct from `.no`. Correct tri-state.
- `WitnessView.swift:14-50` — eleven distinct verdict states, green reserved for `.valid`, and
  `.untrustedSigner` correctly red rather than green. The single-verdict-row discipline (:243) is
  exactly what GluttonView's signature block lacks.
- `OverallVerdictView.swift:277-302` — `stateColor` / `stateHeadline`: `.inconclusive` and
  `.untested` both `.ioInfoPurple`, never green. Correct.
- `MirrorView.swift:285-318` — resolver-comparison verdict distinguishes inconclusive / redirection /
  degraded / clean, skips failed outcomes when computing disagreements, and names the differing
  answers. This is what ProphetView's consensus should look like.
- `SettingsView.swift:179-192` — five honest encrypted-DNS states including "Treated as NOT
  protected until confirmed".
- `DashboardView.swift:459-502` — the activity terminal renders only strings production code really
  emitted, with an honest empty state.
- `RemoteContentView.swift:136-180` — every load failure renders a diagnosed page; the comment at
  :142-144 is the correct statement of the doctrine.

**[E124]** W3-01 — ConclusionsView still renders the retired DST verdict/confidence/referral fields
**Criticality:** CRITICAL (compile break + fabricated confidence)
**Location:** `Windows/dotNET/SyxxUI/Views/ConclusionsView.xaml.cs:40-46`
**Issue:** `Conclusion` (`Syxx.Kit/Synthesis/Conclusion.cs:22-29`) has exactly five members —
`GeneratedAt`, `SectionStatuses`, `Evidence`, `Advisories`, `Determination`. Its own header
(`Conclusion.cs:19-20`) lists `Confidence`, `Referral`, `Stage5` as *removed by the matrix cutover*.
`ConclusionsView` still reads `conclusion.Verdict`, `conclusion.Confidence`, `conclusion.Referral`
and calls a `Title()` extension on `Verdict`. None exist: there is no `Conclusion.Verdict`, no
`Referral` type anywhere in `Syxx.Kit` (only `VantageComparer.Verdict`, an unrelated nested class at
`VantageComparer.cs:287`), and no `Title()` extension. Four CS1061s in seven lines. The same file's
own migration note (`:247-266`) claims this view *was* re-derived onto `DeterminativeResult` — it was
re-derived only below line 61; the header block was left on the dead DTO. Doctrine layer: even if it
compiled, `Confidence: {n}%` is precisely the fabricated synthesized confidence the owner directive
(2026-07-21) removed engine-side; re-printing it in the GUI resurrects it.
**Cross-ref. Delta:** MATRIX-MIGRATION-PLAN Ph3.3 / Ph3.6; the D092/D101 "no CI can compile SyxxUI" class.
**Fix(es):** Delete lines 40-46. `VerdictText` ← `conclusion.Determination?.State` in the engine's
vocabulary (the mapping `DashboardView.xaml.cs:52-59` already has), or `ReportCards.For(c).Headline`.
Delete `ConfidenceText` and its XAML block (`ConclusionsView.xaml:54-56`) outright — no substitute
number exists. Delete `ReferralText` and `ConclusionsView.xaml:57-59`.
**Code Sample:**
```csharp
// ConclusionsView.xaml.cs:40-46
VerdictText.Text = $"Verdict: {conclusion.Verdict.Title()}";
ConfidenceText.Text = $"Confidence: {conclusion.Confidence}%";
ReferralText.Text = conclusion.Referral is not null
    ? $"Referral: {conclusion.Referral.Reason} ({string.Join(", ", conclusion.Referral.Subreddits)})"
    : "";
```
**FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** Replaced retired Verdict/Confidence/Referral fields with Determination.State; removed ConfidenceText and ReferralText XAML elements.

