**[E126]** W3-03 — `SyxxSettings.NotificationsEnabled` read as a static; it is an instance property
**Criticality:** CRITICAL (compile break) — and it silences the only drift notification path
**Location:** `Windows/dotNET/SyxxUI/ViewModels/AppViewModel.cs:94`
**Issue:** `SyxxSettings` is a plain settings DTO — `Syxx.Kit/SyxxSettings.cs:17-32` declares
`public bool NotificationsEnabled { get; set; } = true;` as an **instance** member; the loader is the
separate `SyxxSettingsStore.Load()`. The monitor tick reads it off the *type*. CS0120
("an object reference is required for the non-static field"). `SettingsView.xaml.cs:16` gets this
right (`SyxxSettingsStore.Load()` into `_settings`); the view-model does not.
**Cross-ref. Delta:** A5/D-4 toast delivery.
**Fix(es):** Load once per tick (cheap, and picks up a mid-session Settings change):
`if (tick.State == MonitorState.Changed && SyxxSettingsStore.Load().NotificationsEnabled)`.
**Code Sample:**
```csharp
// AppViewModel.cs:94
if (tick.State == MonitorState.Changed && SyxxSettings.NotificationsEnabled)
```
**FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** Changed to load settings fresh on each tick using SyxxSettingsStore.Load().NotificationsEnabled to pick up mid-session changes.

