**[E134]** W3-11 — Dashboard "QUERIES SEEN" card is unconditionally green, including when it reads "—"
**FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** Changed QueriesCard border to blue when data present, neutral when empty; counts are facts not verdicts.

**Criticality:** HIGH (clean is the only green — this is green for untested)
**Location:** `Windows/dotNET/SyxxUI/Views/DashboardView.xaml.cs:81-82`
**Issue:** `QueriesCard.BorderBrush = BorderTint("IoSuccessGreenColor");` is outside every branch.
`QueriesText` is "—" whenever `CageEventsCount == 0` (i.e. no capture has ever run), and the card is
still tinted success-green. Every other card on the row is state-driven —
`AlertsCard` (`:65`), `LeakCard` (`:74-79`), `ConfidenceCard` (`:60`) — so this is a single missed
line, but it is the only green thing on the pane at first launch. The file's own `VerdictBorder`
doc (`:88-90`) states the rule it violates.
**Cross-ref. Delta:** B088.
**Fix(es):** `QueriesCard.BorderBrush = BorderTint(_vm.CageEventsCount > 0 ? "IoBlueColor" : "IoTextSecondaryColor");`
— a count is a fact, not a verdict, so it should not be graded green at all.
**Code Sample:**
```csharp
// DashboardView.xaml.cs:81-82
QueriesText.Text = _vm.CageEventsCount > 0 ? _vm.CageEventsCount.ToString() : "—";
QueriesCard.BorderBrush = BorderTint("IoSuccessGreenColor");
```

