**[E135]** W3-12 — Dashboard card labelled "CONFIDENCE" now shows a verdict word, not a confidence
**Criticality:** HIGH (label contradicts content; screen readers announce a number that isn't there)
**Location:** `Windows/dotNET/SyxxUI/Views/DashboardView.xaml:57-72` vs `Views/DashboardView.xaml.cs:45-60`
**Issue:** The code-behind was correctly migrated — it now writes `"Clean" / "Threat" / "Unresolved" /
"Not tested" / "—"` and explains at `:47-50` that the engine produces no confidence percentage. The
XAML was not: the caption is still `Text="CONFIDENCE"` (`:68`), the automation name is still
`AutomationProperties.Name="Confidence score"` (`:63`), and the XAML comment at `:57-60` still
asserts "the number is the engine's confidence in its NAMED verdict". A user (and any assistive
technology) is told the word "Threat" is a confidence score. Parity note: the macOS
`DashboardView.swift` has no such stat-grid at all (it is the Watchtower redesign), so the repeated
"parity with macOS DashboardView" comments in this file (`:12`, `:25`) are stale.
**Cross-ref. Delta:** B088; matrix cutover Ph3.
**Fix(es):** Rename to `VERDICT`, `AutomationProperties.Name="Network verdict"`, delete the stale
