**[E136]** W3-13 — License activation never unlocks Pro in the running session
**Criticality:** HIGH (real functional bug + false promise in accessibility copy)
**Location:** `Windows/dotNET/SyxxUI/Views/LicenseView.xaml.cs:50-92` (esp. `:59`, `:91`) ·
`:22` · `:94-97` · `Views/DashboardView.xaml:221-229`
**Issue:** Three defects on the commerce path.
(1) A successful activation sets `_vm.LicenseKey` (`:59`) and reports success (`:74-77`), but never
sets `_vm.IsPro`. `RefreshStatusAsync()` (`:91`) only rewrites a label. Since `IsPro` is only ever
assigned in `AppViewModel.CheckLicenseAsync()` (called at launch), Mirror stays hard-refused
(W3-07) until the app is restarted — after the UI has said "License activated. Pro features are
unlocked on this machine."
(2) `CheckoutUrl` (`:22`) is computed from `SyxxConfig.DimensionBaseURL` and **never referenced**.
`TrialBtn_Click` (`:94-97`) opens the bare homepage `https://syxx.app`, while the button's
`AutomationProperties.HelpText` (`LicenseView.xaml:105`) promises "Opens the checkout page to begin a
three-day free trial". The Dashboard's `ProUpgradeBtn` (`DashboardView.xaml:221-229`) likewise
navigates to `https://syxx.app` with HelpText "Opens the checkout page to begin a Pro trial".
(3) `ProUpgradeBtn`'s `x:Name` is never used in code-behind — dead handle.
**Cross-ref. Delta:** E028, D042, D043.
**Fix(es):** After `LicenseValidationResult.Valid`, `await _vm.CheckLicenseAsync()` (or set
`_vm.IsPro = true` directly) before `RefreshStatusAsync()`. Point `TrialBtn_Click` at `CheckoutUrl`
(or delete `CheckoutUrl` and correct both HelpText strings to "Opens syxx.app").
**Code Sample:**
```csharp
// LicenseView.xaml.cs:22 — never referenced
private static string CheckoutUrl => $"{SyxxConfig.DimensionBaseURL.TrimEnd('/')}/api/checkout?sku=syxx_win_yearly_sub";
// :94-97
private void TrialBtn_Click(object sender, RoutedEventArgs e)
    => _ = Launcher.LaunchUriAsync(new Uri(SyxxUrl));   // SyxxUrl == "https://syxx.app"
```
**FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code), already resolved.** ActivateBtn_Click now calls RefreshStatusAsync() which sets _vm.IsPro; TrialBtn_Click now uses CheckoutUrl.

