**[E139]** W3-16 — Conclusions shows stale evidence cards *and* "No checks have been run yet." after Reset
**Criticality:** HIGH (evidence from a previous run presented as current; self-contradicting pane)
**Location:** `Windows/dotNET/SyxxUI/Views/ConclusionsView.xaml.cs:64-161` (esp. `:74-76`, `:160`) ·
`:174-179`
**Issue:** In the `conclusion is null` branch every component card is only ever set to
`Visibility.Visible`; none is ever set back to `Collapsed`. `ResetBtn_Click` runs `ResetAllCommand`
(which does `SectionInputs = new()`, `AppViewModel.cs:419`) and calls `Refresh()`. All the
`inputs.X is not null` tests now fail, so the cards keep their previous visibility **and their
previous text** — Prophet/Mirror/Portal/Glutton/Cage/Witness details from the wiped session stay on
screen. Simultaneously `anyData` is `false`, so `EmptyStateText` — "No checks have been run yet." —
is made visible directly beneath them. The pane asserts both. Same path fires from the sidebar
"Start your story anew" (`MainWindow.xaml.cs:154-158`) followed by any navigation back to
Conclusions.
**Cross-ref. Delta:** macOS `AppModel.resetAll()` twin.
**Fix(es):** At the top of the `else` branch, collapse all seven cards
(`ProphetCard`…`WitnessCard`) and clear their `*Detail.Text` before the population pass; also
collapse `ActionCard`, `ExplanationCard`, `Stage5Card` in that branch (they are only ever shown, at
`:55`, `:59`, `:269`).
**Code Sample:**
```csharp
// ConclusionsView.xaml.cs:74-76 — visibility is only ever turned ON
if (inputs.Resolution is not null)
{
    ProphetCard.Visibility = Visibility.Visible;
// :160
EmptyStateText.Visibility = anyData ? Visibility.Collapsed : Visibility.Visible;
```

**FIXED 2026-07-30 (qwen-code).** Added explicit collapse and text clearing of all component cards at the start of the null-conclusion branch to prevent stale data after Reset.

