## C. DEAD UI, PARITY, AND CORRECTNESS

---

**[E146]** W3-23 — Prophet's record-type picker is decorative; every lookup is A/AAAA regardless
**Criticality:** HIGH (the user selects MX and is shown A records under a neutral label)
**Location:** `Windows/dotNET/SyxxUI/Views/ProphetView.xaml:53-60` · `ViewModels/AppViewModel.cs:21, 35-36, 416` ·
`Syxx.Kit/ProbePlan.cs:31`
**Issue:** `RecordTypePicker` has no `SelectionChanged`, no `x:Bind`, and no reference in
`ProphetView.xaml.cs`. `AppViewModel.RecordType` (`:21`) is written only by `ResetAll` (`:416`) and
read by nothing. `AppViewModel.RecordTypes` (`:35-36`, ten types) is bound by nothing — the ComboBox
hardcodes six different items. And the probe entry point has no record-type parameter at all:
`ProbePlan.RunProphetAsync(string domain, string resolver, bool includeAAAA = true)`. So selecting
"MX" changes nothing, and the results header (`ProphetView.xaml.cs:64-65`,
"Returned DNS records for {domain}:") gives no hint that the answer is not the requested type.
**Cross-ref. Delta:** —
**Fix(es):** Shortest honest fix: remove the picker (and `RecordType`/`RecordTypes`) until the Kit
supports it. Otherwise thread a type through `ProbePlan.RunProphetAsync` → `DNSResolver`, bind
`ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.RecordTypes}"` + `SelectedItem` to `RecordType`, set
`SectionInputs.TargetQueryType` (`Synthesizer.cs:24`, currently never set on Windows), and put the
type in the results label.
**Code Sample:**
```xml
<!-- ProphetView.xaml:53-60 — no binding, no handler -->
<ComboBox Grid.Column="2" x:Name="RecordTypePicker" Width="110" SelectedIndex="0">
    <ComboBoxItem>A</ComboBoxItem> ... <ComboBoxItem>CNAME</ComboBoxItem>
</ComboBox>
```

