**Criticality:** MEDIUM
**Location:** `Windows/dotNET/SyxxUI/Styles/IoDesignSystem.xaml:39, 41` (and `42` vs `33`)
**Issue:** `IoWarningAmberColor` and `IoHighOrangeColor` are both `#FFF7931E`.
`Presentation/SeverityBrush.cs:14-15` promises "Warning→amber, High→orange (NOT red)" as distinct
grades, and `CageView`'s badge mapping (`CageView.xaml.cs:377-385`) relies on them differing —
`ExfilSuspicion.Suspicious → Severity.Warning` vs a `High` finding render identically. Same for
`IoInfoPurpleColor` == `IoElectricColor` (`#FFA78BFF`), which makes an Info severity badge
indistinguishable from ordinary Mirror/Prophet accent chrome.
**Cross-ref. Delta:** SeverityBrush.
**Fix(es):** Give `IoHighOrangeColor` a genuinely distinct orange (e.g. `#FFFF7A1A`) and confirm the
five severity swatches are separable at 6px (the badge dot size, `CageView.xaml:157`). Mirror any
change into the macOS `Color.ioSeverity` twin so the two clients stay identical.
