**[E152]** W3-29 — "Dimensions" nav item stays selected while the content pane shows something else
**Criticality:** LOW-MEDIUM
**Location:** `Windows/dotNET/SyxxUI/MainWindow.xaml.cs:160-168`
**Issue:** The `"Dimensions"` branch launches the browser and `return`s without navigating — but
`NavigationView` has already committed the selection, so the sidebar highlights Dimensions
indefinitely while `ContentFrame` still shows the previous pane. Clicking Dimensions a second time
raises no `SelectionChanged` (already selected), so the external link becomes a one-shot. Also
`NavView.SelectedItem = NavView.MenuItems[0]` in the constructor (`:55`) fires `SelectionChanged`
and re-navigates to `RemoteContentPanel`, which `:54` just navigated to — a duplicate page
construction and a duplicate `FetchWhatsNewUrl()`/WebView2 init at every launch.
**Cross-ref. Delta:** —
**Fix(es):** Restore the prior selection before returning (cache the last navigated tag and reassign
`sender.SelectedItem`), or make Dimensions a `NavigationViewItem` with `SelectsOnInvoked="False"` and
an `ItemInvoked` handler — the pattern already used by the "Start your story anew" pill
(`MainWindow.xaml:305`). Drop either `:54` or `:55`.
**Code Sample:**
```csharp
// MainWindow.xaml.cs:163-168
if (item.Tag as string == "Dimensions")
{
    _ = Launcher.LaunchUriAsync(new Uri("https://syxx.app"));
    return;                     // selection stays on Dimensions
}
```

