**[E157]** W3-34 — Stage-5 reasoning prints CLR enum identifiers to the user
**Criticality:** LOW
**Location:** `Views/ConclusionsView.xaml.cs:302, 313`
**Issue:** `$"{d.DisplayName}: {d.Confidence}"` renders `DiagnosisConfidence.ToString()` and
`$"({s.Reason}) {s.DisplayName}"` renders `SuppressedDiagnosis.SuppressionReason.ToString()` — so the
user sees `"MissingRequiredSection"`, `"BelowTier"`, `"HardExcluded"`. The Kit ships the intended
strings: `DiagnosisConfidence.RawValue()` (`MatrixDeterminativeEngine.cs:521`) and the
`SuppressionReasonJsonConverter` vocabulary (`:641-649`). `det.State.RawValue()` is used correctly
one line up at `:288`.
**Fix(es):** Use `d.Confidence.RawValue()`; add a human-readable `Describe()` for
`SuppressionReason` ("required check never ran", "below the confidence threshold", …) rather than a
camel-case token.

