**[E160]** W3-37 — `CheckLicenseAsync` fires twice at launch; `OnSuspending` never runs unpackaged
**Criticality:** LOW
**Location:** `App.xaml.cs:69-82` · `MainWindow.xaml.cs:58-60`
**Issue:** `MainWindow`'s constructor (`:60`) and `App.OnLaunched` (`:74`) both start
`ViewModel.CheckLicenseAsync()` — two concurrent Keygen round-trips, two `lastValidValidation`
writes, and two racing writes to `IsPro`. Separately, `App.Suspending` (`:19`, `:77-82`) does not
fire for an unpackaged Win32 desktop app (`WindowsPackageType=None`, `SyxxUI.csproj:19`), so the
OTel `ForceFlush` and `_sentry.Dispose()` never execute — in-flight spans are lost at exit.
**Fix(es):** Keep one call (`App.OnLaunched`). Flush from `MainWindow.Closed` (`:43`) instead of
`Suspending`, or additionally from `AppDomain.CurrentDomain.ProcessExit`.

