- **[F043]**               The Ubuntu Third of the Three-Platform Witness Parity Harness Is Never Compiled or Run by CI
- **Criticality:**      Critical
- **Location:**         .github/workflows/ci.yml:74-102 (no step targets it);
                        Windows/Syxx.Linux.slnf (lists Syxx.Kit, Syxx, Syxx.Tests only);
                        Ubuntu/SyxxUI.Avalonia.Tests/WitnessTestifyParityTests.cs,
                        Ubuntu/SyxxUI.Avalonia.Tests/WitnessViewModelTests.cs
- **Issue:**            The shared fixture's own note
                        (corpus/witness-testify-parity/witness-testify-parity.json:2) defines the
                        harness as three loaders — macOS `WitnessTestifyParityTests.swift`, Windows
                        `WitnessTestifyParityTests.cs`, and
                        `Ubuntu/SyxxUI.Avalonia.Tests/WitnessTestifyParityTests.cs` — each asserting
                        its own platform against the single source of truth. CI runs the first two
                        (ci.yml:98 for SyxxUI.Tests, :102 for Syxx.Tests, :116 for Swift). The Ubuntu
                        leg builds `Syxx.Linux.slnf`, which does not contain
                        `SyxxUI.Avalonia.Tests.csproj`; no `dotnet test` step names it. The project is
                        in no solution or filter that CI touches. Its last recorded execution is a
                        manual one quoted in `SYXX-PUBLICATION-READINESS-AUDIT-2026-07-24.md:912`
                        ("7 passed"), which is a snapshot, not a gate.
                        Effect: "three-platform Witness parity" is asserted by two platforms. An
                        Ubuntu-only divergence in `WitnessViewModel`'s pre-flight guards — exactly the
                        deliberately-divergent per-platform layer D103 records — cannot be caught by
                        any automated run.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** D103; MATRIX-MIGRATION-PLAN.md:327 plans to ADD more tests to this
                        never-executed project.
- **Fix(es):**          Add `Ubuntu/SyxxUI.Avalonia.Tests/SyxxUI.Avalonia.Tests.csproj` to
                        `Syxx.Linux.slnf` and add a `dotnet test` step on the `ubuntu-x64` leg.

