- **[F045]**               Four `MatrixDeterminativeEngineTests` Assertions Are `if let`/negative-only and Survive Deletion of the Behaviour They Name
- **Criticality:**      Non-critical
- **Location:**         macOS/Tests/SyxxKitTests/MatrixDeterminativeEngineTests.swift:668-719,
                        :617-661, :823-853, :490-509
- **Issue:**            • `testRequireDecisiveOrTwoMajors_minorsOnlyReachesProbableNotConclusive`
                          (:668-719): the body is `if let top = result.diagnoses.first { …probable… }
                          else { XCTAssertNotEqual(result.state, .threatDetected) }` (:706-715), and
                          the closing assertion is
                          `XCTAssertFalse(result.diagnoses.contains { $0.confidence == .conclusive })`
                          (:717) — vacuously true on an empty list. Delete the emission path entirely
                          and this test is green. The `else` comment (:711-713) states the widening
                          explicitly: "If it didn't even reach probable, that's also valid."
                        • `testContradictionBounded_attenuatesNeverZeroes` (:617-661): same `if let`/
                          `else` shape (:650-660). The test's own thesis is "contradiction must not
                          zero the threat — bounded attenuation" (:653-654), and the `else` branch
                          accepts the threat being zeroed out of emission, which is the thesis's
                          negation. (The `else` is at least tight: it pins `.inconclusive` and
                          requires the diagnosis in `suppressed`.)
                        • `testHardGate_inconclusiveSectionDoesNotGate` (:823-853): asserts only
                          `XCTAssertFalse(isGated)` (:852). It never asserts the diagnosis actually
                          emits, so it passes if `notGated` is suppressed for any *other* reason, or
                          if the engine stops evaluating the diagnosis at all — the pure `!= X`
                          shape. Its sibling `testHardExclusion_belowThresholdDoesNotSuppress`
                          (:490-509) does it correctly, asserting the positive
                          (`diagnoses.contains { … "dnsSpoofing" }`, :507).
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** none.
- **Fix(es):**          Replace each `if let`/`else` with an unconditional `XCTUnwrap` of the
                        diagnosis and a pinned confidence tier; add
                        `XCTAssertTrue(result.diagnoses.contains { $0.id.rawValue == "notGated" })`
                        to `testHardGate_inconclusiveSectionDoesNotGate`.

