                          • `TrayIndicators` (Sources/SyxxKit/Synthesis/TrayIndicator.swift:42) —
                            **zero** active tests. Its only tests are `_quarantine/TrayGlyphTests.swift`
                            and `_quarantine/SoWhatLayerTests.swift:148,156,169`. The menu-bar trust
                            indicator ships with no test of any kind.
                          • `FirstRunScan` (Sources/SyxxKit/Synthesis/FirstRunScan.swift AND
                            Sources/SyxxCLI/Synthesis/FirstRunScan.swift) — **zero** active macOS
                            tests, while the Windows twin `Syxx.Tests/FirstRunScanTests.cs` IS in CI.
                            One-sided parity: the same feature is guarded on Windows and unguarded on
                            macOS.
                          • `DNSCanaries` (Sources/SyxxKit/Synthesis/DNSCanaries.swift, 118 lines,
                            called from ProbePlan.swift:44) — **zero** tests, active or quarantined.
                          • `ReportCards` / `VerdictActions` — active coverage exists in exactly one
                            file, `MatrixUntestedStateTests.swift`, which `git status --porcelain`
                            reports as `??` (untracked). If it is not committed, both render paths
                            revert to zero coverage.
                        The subjects of most other quarantined files (`Synthesizer.swift`,
                        `SynthesisEngine.swift`, `Conclusion.swift`, `Report.swift`,
                        `PlainExplanation.swift`, `MonitorReportAnalyzer.swift`,
                        `EncryptedDNSConfig.swift`) are all still present in `macOS/Sources/`, so this
                        is not "tests for deleted code" — it is live code with its guards switched off.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** MATRIX-MIGRATION-PLAN.md:183 plans a REWRITE of `Stage0GoldenCorpusTests`
                        only; it does not authorise the other 18 files' removal from the build.
- **Fix(es):**          Triage the 19 files against still-shipping subjects. For each: restore to the
                        test target and accept the red, or delete the file with an explicit
                        cross-reference to the deleted subject. `_quarantine` as a permanent,
                        unreferenced, uncompiled directory is the worst of both — the guards look
                        present in the tree and enforce nothing. Minimum immediate action: restore
                        `TrayGlyphTests` (see prior finding), `MonitorReportAnalyzerTests` and
                        `FirstRunScanTests`, whose subjects ship and whose Windows twins are tested.

