- **[B241]**               M6-14 · Baseline "saved" Messages Printed Over Discarded `try?` Writes
- **Criticality:**      Medium; the user is told a trust baseline was persisted when the write may
                        have failed. A Sentinel with no baseline reports "no change" forever.
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxCLI/Commands/SyxxSentinel.swift:24, :43, :48, :63;
                        macOS/Sources/SyxxCLI/SyxxCLI.swift:771 (guided Witness);
                        throwing APIs: macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/Trust/Sentinel.swift:82, :144
- **Issue:**            `Sentinel.saveSnapshot` and `HomeBaseline.save` both `throw`
                        (Sentinel.swift:82, :144). Every call site in the CLI swallows the error
                        with `try?` and prints an unconditional success line:
                        "🏠 Saved this network as your home baseline." (:24-25),
                        "Baseline reset. Future runs will compare against this snapshot." (:43-44),
                        "No prior baseline — saved this snapshot as the baseline." (:48-49), the
                        silent roll-forward at :63, and the guided Witness
                        "• No prior baseline — this snapshot is now the trusted baseline."
                        (SyxxCLI.swift:769-771). On a read-only home, a full disk, or a sandbox
                        denial the message is false and the *next* run silently re-reports "no
                        prior baseline" — drift detection is dead while claiming to be armed.
                        Doctrine: an operation must not report success it did not verify.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** None found for these call sites. Class precedent: **D052**
                        (AppModel.swift:1478-1498) fixed exactly this pattern for the Keychain
                        write — the CLI was not swept.
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] `do { try Sentinel.saveSnapshot(current); print("…saved…") }
                        catch { print("⚠️ Baseline NOT saved: \(error.localizedDescription) —
                        drift detection is not armed.") }` at all five sites.
                        [Fix 2] Set the error exit code (see M6-05) when a baseline write fails.
                        [Fix 3] On the compare path, verify the snapshot re-reads before claiming
                        the baseline is established.
- **Code Sample:**      [

                        // Commands/SyxxSentinel.swift:42-44
                        if args.contains("--reset") {
                            try? Sentinel.saveSnapshot(current)
                            print("\nBaseline reset. Future runs will compare against this snapshot.")

                        // SyxxKit/Trust/Sentinel.swift:82 — it throws for a reason
                        public static func saveSnapshot(_ snapshot: NetworkConfigSnapshot, to url: URL = Sentinel.defaultURL) throws {

                        ]

